lamAV daemon is reachable and sized for the added traffic\n  before deploying. No configuration change is required -- the exemption list is not\n  configurable by design, so it cannot be widened into a bypass at runtime.\n\n`text/x-gwt-rpc` is on the exemption list because the e2e suite proved its absence\nfail-closes the whole authoring UI: every `POST /gwt/*.gwt` answered 503. Unit tests\ncannot catch that class of mistake -- they assert the rule you designed, not the set of\nmedia types Jahia actually uses.\n\nVerification:\n\n  - 176 unit tests (was 129). Mutation-checked: restoring the pre-SEC-418 predicate in\n    place fails 20 of them, so they detect the vulnerability rather than describe the code.\n  - Live A/B using the fiche''s own reproduction and its own discriminator (the\n    fail-closed log-line delta, never the HTTP status), on 8.2.3.2 with clamd deliberately\n    unreachable: all three positive controls fired, and all five shapes the fiche measured\n    as SCANNED=0 on 1.0.4 are now SCANNED=1. The exemptions and bodyless requests are\n    SCANNED=0. SEC-418 no longer reproduces.\n  - Docker Cypress suite green: 33/33, all 5 specs.\n  - OSGi Import-Package unchanged (the MediaType.*_VALUE constants inline at compile time).\n\nAlso included, both pre-existing and unrelated to the security change:\n\n  - build: the pinned node was raised v22.6.0 -> v22.11.0. The module could not be built\n    at all -- the locked sass-loader@17.0.0 requires node >= 22.11.0 and Yarn Classic\n    treats the engine mismatch as fatal, so `yarn install` aborted before webpack ran.\n  - tests: `cypress/support/bindFetch.js` binds fetch before @jahia/cypress pulls in\n    cross-fetch, whose browser build re-exports the native fetch detached from the window\n    (`exports = ctx.fetch`, browser-ponyfill.js:678). Apollo''s HttpLink called it bare, so\n    every `cy.apollo()` failed with \"Illegal invocation\" -- 13 failures that looked like a\n    broken module. The proper fix belongs upstream in Jahia/jahia-cypress.\n  - tests: provisioning now points the module at the `clamav` service before any spec\n    runs, removing a cross-spec dependency where a failed saveSettings silently degraded\n    403 scan assertions into 503.\n  - tests: ci.startup.sh now forwards \"$@\", so the documented `./ci.startup.sh notests`\n    works instead of running the whole suite.\n\nNote: this repository has no build or test CI workflow (only .github/dependabot.yml plus\norg-level CodeQL), which is why the broken node pin, the broken Apollo client and the\ndropped ci.startup.sh argument all went unnoticed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsTXPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMNYQAGKXDUfKayucnhHlmr8rnoS1\nXVREiPm//p7+9rl47imomIG7t779/sTXDHVwyv80RHnFOa56eu9BHAVeuPRX/rGs\nxLtY9E63N8MwQrpb1dyODTQzw3a27TV+HgcpeliHNsrqry1BnvyYvhkOGMqtbr2i\n4NzDalktOG77VqdkhTjXFitjFArvCLotE9bbF5z4ixSHyApmBra1Wr7NiRTZGx3I\nOSRocGiMZS9pqsfCi0Z1EjkQpXeb5d10aNfBhvHZxf6QpA9Mnw+N20b7wWbHShBQ\nNo5bw+QBAvuo3teBmQ02Edoi69LuGYZcrEMopQ+REHJCsm2d52YeIotYF1/TneJI\nDYnKTm+QmJTeeb+EEdyUgERPWLFnqjunLPBwfLCTCN4PEyU0Y2crC7LARZK/FbT3\nNeZgg3JGIoUUDXBrD5d0BkoPU/i9Mx7SKuUIrG7bziL1YpEkdbl7TygteeAj8AFI\n/n9e9OrDRmEgHgZ8RLIeLM8Q+z6Gmeb1jJ4/84o3pVJK1g6PKvbG7MJSlfvm8GAw\nKN5OEpJUqxniXSGzIYWhTNTPE4b6vhWr6krpk7EvKb3IHrfA74djtg5wbenfhMpb\ni3RMCLRhx8giFY6UeKeLPLhWbfFzUyDtO9PCX9Gz2Mc6RiNDXyaMGfloqa4Zlcim\ndigYabuQ93U7C9zWWQvw\n=wYoT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T13:49:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/f6a65fefc48bc6ee1635900e7811ae375dc916f3","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGY2YTY1ZmVmYzQ4YmM2ZWUxNjM1OTAwZTc4MTFhZTM3NWRjOTE2ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288","sha":"d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288"}],"sha":"f6a65fefc48bc6ee1635900e7811ae375dc916f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/f6a65fefc48bc6ee1635900e7811ae375dc916f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:32:42Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:32:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(tests): make `tsc --noEmit` clean and add a typecheck script (#59)\n\n`tsc` was unusable in this workspace, so nothing type-checked the Cypress\nspecs. Fixed in three layers, then wired to a script so it cannot rot again.\n\n1. skipLibCheck. tsconfig `include` pulls in node_modules/cypress, so Cypress''s\n   own .d.ts files were type-checked — including its optional react/svelte/vue\n   component adapters, whose peer types (@types/react, svelte, vue) this\n   harness neither has nor should install. That produced dozens of\n   TS2307/TS7016 errors from inside node_modules and buried everything real.\n\n2. types: [\"cypress\", \"node\"]. The specs are CommonJS: they use webpack''s\n   inline-loader require syntax (require(''graphql-tag/loader!../fixtures/...'')),\n   resolved at bundle time by @cypress/webpack-preprocessor. TypeScript 6 no\n   longer pulls @types/node''s globals in implicitly here, so all 8 of those\n   calls reported TS2591 \"Cannot find name ''require''\" even though @types/node\n   26.1.1 is installed.\n\n   Naming the type packages explicitly is deliberate: the other way to restore\n   the `require` global is moduleResolution:\"node\", which does work but emits\n   TS5107 (deprecated in TS 6, removed in TS 7) — a fix with a built-in expiry\n   date. This has none.\n\n3. The `(result: never)` escape hatch, 6 sites across 02 and 04. cy.apollo\n   yields ApolloQueryResult | FetchResult, so a `never` callback parameter is\n   not assignable and current typings reject it (TS2769). Replaced with an\n   `errorsOf(result: unknown)` helper that narrows internally, letting the\n   callbacks keep their inferred types. Data reads go through\n   `as unknown as {...}` since the real union no longer overlaps those shapes\n   directly.\n\nResult: 0 tsc errors, down from 14 (plus the node_modules noise). Adds a\n`typecheck` script (`tsc --noEmit`) so this is runnable and discoverable\nrather than only reachable by hand.\n\nType-level only — annotations are erased at runtime, so no spec behaviour\nchanges. Also refreshes 04''s docblock, which still claimed README/AGENTS\ndocumented the flat API; AGENTS.md was corrected in e6aeff5, so the canary and\nthe docs now agree.\n\nVerified: yarn typecheck (0 errors), yarn lint clean in both workspaces\n(prettier/prettier caught my long lines, fixed via lint:fix), root yarn test\n36 Jest tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"544fc3b33d3426b883240bf7f474f1890fdd51cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/544fc3b33d3426b883240bf7f474f1890fdd51cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288","verification":{"payload":"tree 544fc3b33d3426b883240bf7f474f1890fdd51cb\nparent d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786692762 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786692762 +0200\n\nchore(tests): make `tsc --noEmit` clean and add a typecheck script (#59)\n\n`tsc` was unusable in this workspace, so nothing type-checked the Cypress\nspecs. Fixed in three layers, then wired to a script so it cannot rot again.\n\n1. skipLibCheck. tsconfig `include` pulls in node_modules/cypress, so Cypress''s\n   own .d.ts files were type-checked — including its optional react/svelte/vue\n   component adapters, whose peer types (@types/react, svelte, vue) this\n   harness neither has nor should install. That produced dozens of\n   TS2307/TS7016 errors from inside node_modules and buried everything real.\n\n2. types: [\"cypress\", \"node\"]. The specs are CommonJS: they use webpack''s\n   inline-loader require syntax (require(''graphql-tag/loader!../fixtures/...'')),\n   resolved at bundle time by @cypress/webpack-preprocessor. TypeScript 6 no\n   longer pulls @types/node''s globals in implicitly here, so all 8 of those\n   calls reported TS2591 \"Cannot find name ''require''\" even though @types/node\n   26.1.1 is installed.\n\n   Naming the type packages explicitly is deliberate: the other way to restore\n   the `require` global is moduleResolution:\"node\", which does work but emits\n   TS5107 (deprecated in TS 6, removed in TS 7) — a fix with a built-in expiry\n   date. This has none.\n\n3. The `(result: never)` escape hatch, 6 sites across 02 and 04. cy.apollo\n   yields ApolloQueryResult | FetchResult, so a `never` callback parameter is\n   not assignable and current typings reject it (TS2769). Replaced with an\n   `errorsOf(result: unknown)` helper that narrows internally, letting the\n   callbacks keep their inferred types. Data reads go through\n   `as unknown as {...}` since the real union no longer overlaps those shapes\n   directly.\n\nResult: 0 tsc errors, down from 14 (plus the node_modules noise). Adds a\n`typecheck` script (`tsc --noEmit`) so this is runnable and discoverable\nrather than only reachable by hand.\n\nType-level only — annotations are erased at runtime, so no spec behaviour\nchanges. Also refreshes 04''s docblock, which still claimed README/AGENTS\ndocumented the flat API; AGENTS.md was corrected in e6aeff5, so the canary and\nthe docs now agree.\n\nVerified: yarn typecheck (0 errors), yarn lint clean in both workspaces\n(prettier/prettier caught my long lines, fixed via lint:fix), root yarn test\n36 Jest tests.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfsSaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnysQAHpeF3TCky8TKYn9ZKoRX00A\nm4yngxzcXjuRMFUa3XNc6Yt9B9mSr/TZNUb0KOYf3QTM+9ATudiFp4InqOrS6pec\n8tWefRwdmH9McmLtLkVuwkTe3qSUlzVnv2Y5XoNsW82n2EMZxLcMzybXiAW7/wMp\n0AyYrTuIZnzXw4XNE1eSAnhoegu5+561/L5mOcPXMWxWR7FdRDk+/V/qCWLANH6h\numFrBANQOy4Nh54CgzhYqKrbfa4/O56D2VI26Xrgcu5WCgJNvPYeKeMqMDougxwr\nGO4aHhI1en2wrzFxGAz3rEsa6ceoqG46qYeTLptGGf/XWFte7GJA3DVlWMwaEQ9q\nkfHS1F4bzx6f8xit0QzXfDJNzI++X0z4G7V1DbA4CG9BuA9Laantmjd615X2fQ5r\nvyFhJcj4fDQ5BG1wBoOt3dFYMbJNWJD+ghxpNqTP4VGfKWX3AXNWCShGPcBf8fal\nbtqNeUST36/255AAIj/J8P5KfcR702HS/iK4MqTc23fTEFZ4QpyV6LamhURLvYsl\n6nRexYmWPfUUElnRsUZep5pKW51u6t7R6zkCLmu7BVqz6PKGyXLWUhckUl7o9sNm\nHK0Hr52SlJPhRYr9ig7MdGh6aTFG8vBBsPDvSQjYkh8+hmqJ4jQ3sLhFCJQNydhT\n2lglu/lbwyYGsAOwDBst\n=MJH3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T21:49:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGQ5NzQ5NDdmYWUyNmY5NDJiZmVjNjdhMDZkODkyMzI0YWQ0MjYyODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793","sha":"d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793"}],"sha":"d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d974947fae26f942bfec67a06d892324ad426288"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:24:02Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:24:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build(deps): accept round-2 Dependabot updates, hold babel-jest and moonstone (#58)\n\nSecond Dependabot pass (#47-#57) after version updates started running.\nConsolidated for the same reason as #46: shared lockfiles conflict pairwise.\n\nAccepted — build/test scope only, nothing in the shipped bundle:\n\n  pom.xml   maven-surefire-plugin      3.5.4   -> 3.5.6\n  root      @babel/preset-react        ^7.24.1 -> ^7.29.7\n  root      sass-loader                ^12.4.0 -> ^17.0.0\n  root      rimraf                     ^5.0.0  -> ^6.1.3\n  tests     typescript                 ^4.4.4  -> ^6.0.3\n  tests     cross-fetch                3.1.6   -> 4.1.0\n  tests     supports-color             ^9.0.2  -> ^11.0.0\n  tests     cypress-multi-reporters    ^1.6.3  -> ^2.0.5\n  tests     mochawesome-merge          ^4.2.0  -> ^5.1.1\n\nTwo of these clear problems flagged earlier:\n\n  sass-loader 17 moves off the legacy Sass JS API, so the \"legacy JS API is\n  deprecated and will be removed in Dart Sass 2.0.0\" warning is gone from\n  every build. Verified the CSS Modules output is unchanged — generated class\n  names still follow ClamavFilter__cf_*--<hash>, which the Cypress selectors\n  ([class*=\"cf_...\"]) depend on.\n\n  typescript 6 parses the current @types/node, fixing the TS1005 syntax\n  errors that made `tsc` unusable. It is not fully green yet: tsconfig.json\n  includes node_modules/cypress, so Cypress''s optional react/svelte/vue\n  adapters are type-checked without their peer types. Behind that noise sit\n  14 real pre-existing spec errors — 8x TS2591 (specs call require() with no\n  \"node\" entry in tsconfig types) and 6x the deliberate `(result: never)`\n  escape hatch that current Cypress/Apollo types reject. Left alone here:\n  unrelated to dependencies, and tsc is not wired into any script.\n\nHeld back:\n\n  babel-jest ^29.7.0 -> ^30.4.1 (#50)\n    jest itself stays at ^29.7.0 and no PR moves it, so this is the same\n    incoherent partial upgrade as @babel/core 8: babel-jest 30 targets the\n    jest 30 transform API. Move babel-jest with jest, not before it.\n\n  @jahia/moonstone 2.19.0 -> 2.20.3 (#47)\n    A Module Federation shared singleton, so the declared range becomes a\n    runtime requirement against the Jahia app-shell. The ignore rule added in\n    7e6c453 only covers majors, so minors like this still surface by design —\n    they still need the same deliberate check against the target Jahia.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (129 tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint\nclean in both workspaces, yarn build:production with CSS class names diffed,\ncypress 15.20.1 binary verifies, and the bumped reporter/fetch packages all\nrequire() cleanly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"91f0d67342cbb754a22e05a94fcb24c70d9c2b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/91f0d67342cbb754a22e05a94fcb24c70d9c2b4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793","verification":{"payload":"tree 91f0d67342cbb754a22e05a94fcb24c70d9c2b4e\nparent bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786692242 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786692242 +0200\n\nbuild(deps): accept round-2 Dependabot updates, hold babel-jest and moonstone (#58)\n\nSecond Dependabot pass (#47-#57) after version updates started running.\nConsolidated for the same reason as #46: shared lockfiles conflict pairwise.\n\nAccepted — build/test scope only, nothing in the shipped bundle:\n\n  pom.xml   maven-surefire-plugin      3.5.4   -> 3.5.6\n  root      @babel/preset-react        ^7.24.1 -> ^7.29.7\n  root      sass-loader                ^12.4.0 -> ^17.0.0\n  root      rimraf                     ^5.0.0  -> ^6.1.3\n  tests     typescript                 ^4.4.4  -> ^6.0.3\n  tests     cross-fetch                3.1.6   -> 4.1.0\n  tests     supports-color             ^9.0.2  -> ^11.0.0\n  tests     cypress-multi-reporters    ^1.6.3  -> ^2.0.5\n  tests     mochawesome-merge          ^4.2.0  -> ^5.1.1\n\nTwo of these clear problems flagged earlier:\n\n  sass-loader 17 moves off the legacy Sass JS API, so the \"legacy JS API is\n  deprecated and will be removed in Dart Sass 2.0.0\" warning is gone from\n  every build. Verified the CSS Modules output is unchanged — generated class\n  names still follow ClamavFilter__cf_*--<hash>, which the Cypress selectors\n  ([class*=\"cf_...\"]) depend on.\n\n  typescript 6 parses the current @types/node, fixing the TS1005 syntax\n  errors that made `tsc` unusable. It is not fully green yet: tsconfig.json\n  includes node_modules/cypress, so Cypress''s optional react/svelte/vue\n  adapters are type-checked without their peer types. Behind that noise sit\n  14 real pre-existing spec errors — 8x TS2591 (specs call require() with no\n  \"node\" entry in tsconfig types) and 6x the deliberate `(result: never)`\n  escape hatch that current Cypress/Apollo types reject. Left alone here:\n  unrelated to dependencies, and tsc is not wired into any script.\n\nHeld back:\n\n  babel-jest ^29.7.0 -> ^30.4.1 (#50)\n    jest itself stays at ^29.7.0 and no PR moves it, so this is the same\n    incoherent partial upgrade as @babel/core 8: babel-jest 30 targets the\n    jest 30 transform API. Move babel-jest with jest, not before it.\n\n  @jahia/moonstone 2.19.0 -> 2.20.3 (#47)\n    A Module Federation shared singleton, so the declared range becomes a\n    runtime requirement against the Jahia app-shell. The ignore rule added in\n    7e6c453 only covers majors, so minors like this still surface by design —\n    they still need the same deliberate check against the target Jahia.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (129 tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint\nclean in both workspaces, yarn build:production with CSS class names diffed,\ncypress 15.20.1 binary verifies, and the bumped reporter/fetch packages all\nrequire() cleanly.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfsKSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz9sQALHT+hJY0omdNXUKBq3nQiUa\n7CUOEfVe8B/x9vz9d8yC8b5rVB0p+L0E4CKei85fRmG1Cr7K2pFabHwSM+sv8rxu\nqsfXXQLEv1iivrLgqc5JbQmJ+YY817gikE13VSSzBnJgjBFRfiImBUVoqcKhuQ88\nadi7bHXhXXRCDPAc4oYVceKZw7ePig43wPyCoDzmlWEB0zvW+pcqUrUnGB4Fvr/O\nwJOaasTtz0iF+gsAVZB2RxuNQe2qwvTvYcuU3Amgy+mCTTUbx38VLOVXKveSUqzH\nFTZgBm12+xjzGUBKjp3IqQwV4CyPfRX3EmJM+a8P5GjojE2pBIVIspNwsA53/epJ\np3hn/kVLJnohmavDjzHlgV4DHMkEA8sawEYNKlJNOdc2u/ITGFRu57WlDfW+XJFi\ncp56Fw441okstoRe+y2uz/xQ3eJAofwdZSVCneWz8O+AUrRGLDBSU63uPzvGjQuA\n+eGV1kTcdA83FZdXDtSYLXyJgHOrL6hDA5pg2Dxo/eqcLh8Qv86WDOfshKnYne9a\nhtMTI5v4OxLMqobqnui6cNeY8/tl9BpgEFOOCVopWzQT9SwktEy+lTs42Jofg6kO\nSWJLg59N2sR77Aho4Hg47Sg+82qczWR0wvn/FzgKax/hXJYa5sPXVjtsU55z6m4y\nqx9n+/pss9NSewJ58Qt2\n=TbPu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:24:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGQ1ZDQ1MTYxMTgwMDhkODA3NWQ0YzUzMjlkMmMwY2UzNzE2OTE3OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5","sha":"bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5"}],"sha":"d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/d5d4516118008d8075d4c5329d2c0ce371691793"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:16:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:16:21Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"build: declare yarn 1.22.22 via packageManager in both workspaces\n\nBoth lockfiles are `# yarn lockfile v1`, and frontend-maven-plugin pins\nyarn v1.22.21 for the Maven build — but nothing in the repo told a\ndeveloper''s shell that. With Yarn 4 installed globally, a bare `yarn`\nanywhere in this repo fails with a misleading error:\n\n  Internal Error: clamav-filter-cypress@workspace:.: This package doesn''t\n  seem to be present in your lockfile; run \"yarn install\" to update it\n\nwhich reads like a corrupt lockfile rather than \"you are running the wrong\nYarn major\". The vestigial .yarnrc.yml (Berry-only config, silently ignored\nby Yarn 1) makes it look even more like a Berry project than it is.\n\nDeclaring packageManager lets Corepack select the right Yarn:\n`corepack yarn ...` now resolves 1.22.22 and runs the scripts correctly.\n\nCaveat worth knowing: this alone does not fix a bare `yarn`. Corepack has\nto be in front of it — either run `corepack enable` once, so its shim\nintercepts `yarn`, or call `corepack yarn ...` explicitly. Without that the\nglobal Yarn 4 binary still runs and still ignores this field, because Yarn 4\ndoes not self-downgrade.\n\nVerified with corepack: yarn --version reports 1.22.22 in both workspaces,\n`yarn lint` is clean in tests/, and `yarn test` passes 36 Jest tests at the\nroot. Lockfiles unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"96633be192c609d12ff0a19cee726691c5085133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/96633be192c609d12ff0a19cee726691c5085133"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5","verification":{"payload":"tree 96633be192c609d12ff0a19cee726691c5085133\nparent 4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786691781 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786691781 +0200\n\nbuild: declare yarn 1.22.22 via packageManager in both workspaces\n\nBoth lockfiles are `# yarn lockfile v1`, and frontend-maven-plugin pins\nyarn v1.22.21 for the Maven build — but nothing in the repo told a\ndeveloper''s shell that. With Yarn 4 installed globally, a bare `yarn`\nanywhere in this repo fails with a misleading error:\n\n  Internal Error: clamav-filter-cypress@workspace:.: This package doesn''t\n  seem to be present in your lockfile; run \"yarn install\" to update it\n\nwhich reads like a corrupt lockfile rather than \"you are running the wrong\nYarn major\". The vestigial .yarnrc.yml (Berry-only config, silently ignored\nby Yarn 1) makes it look even more like a Berry project than it is.\n\nDeclaring packageManager lets Corepack select the right Yarn:\n`corepack yarn ...` now resolves 1.22.22 and runs the scripts correctly.\n\nCaveat worth knowing: this alone does not fix a bare `yarn`. Corepack has\nto be in front of it — either run `corepack enable` once, so its shim\nintercepts `yarn`, or call `corepack yarn ...` explicitly. Without that the\nglobal Yarn 4 binary still runs and still ignores this field, because Yarn 4\ndoes not self-downgrade.\n\nVerified with corepack: yarn --version reports 1.22.22 in both workspaces,\n`yarn lint` is clean in tests/, and `yarn test` passes 36 Jest tests at the\nroot. Lockfiles unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+wMUACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3noPAf9FL6H8DQSUaYozUh6flSfuUNGPtDJgTxSqI0GV0UqigebjRZ1p2PASxXT\nVGqc0Kv+mxCYeJyHLY8VGld8buL86KNqLGiGgHxUdkJAAqQKMOiRu9XfLmXUVZwD\neGbJhNSp2rzGxML6lkUuU+dPu3AWXu7e+LOgFeM8ktPhX+9D1CGLQ2Nv1l+DLB9X\nbf6fTRgO3/ZuNT3uHz01SwzAKx3d83qkPTsTWG3siD8IDVv9ydT7zinkGn4137vj\nHyjSNB7DcK2CFT+4C5pFeH2CDEFjK3qJ8jGT6NEANCWMlRqv2/OFkIwxhMl8+cpX\neJl33rimi2H4JuNV1Ixi2PKKhlUTnQ==\n=sblI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:17:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGJhYzgzMWVjZDMyMjc3Mjc1NzJhNTA0ODZlY2YzYzE0NDFkZjZlYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65","sha":"4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65"}],"sha":"bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/bac831ecd3227727572a50486ecf3c1441df6ec5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:15:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:15:08Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"build: move to jahia-modules parent 8.2.3.2, absorbing three regressions it introduces\n\nBumps the Jahia platform baseline from 8.2.1.0 to 8.2.3.2 as requested. The\nnew parent breaks the build in three separate ways, each fixed here; two of\nthem fail silently, which is why each has a comment in the pom.\n\n1. Java level silently drops to 11. The parent sets <release>11</release>\n   inside the default-compile and default-testCompile *execution*\n   configurations, and execution-level config beats the\n   maven.compiler.release/source/target properties this pom already set — so\n   those properties were simply ignored and compilation failed on the\n   pattern-matching instanceof in ClamavFilter.sendError.\n\n   Fixed by overriding the same two execution ids. Only <release> is\n   restated, so Maven''s per-element merge keeps the parent''s\n   annotationProcessorPaths (Lombok). Java 17 is retained deliberately;\n   the bundle is therefore Java 17 bytecode and needs a JDK 17 Jahia.\n\n2. Tests stop running, and the build still passes. The parent declares\n   maven-surefire-plugin 2.22.2 (2019) where 8.2.1.0 declared 3.6.0-M1. With\n   junit-jupiter 6.x the forked JVM dies outright\n   (NoClassDefFoundError: org.junit.platform.commons.util.PreconditionViolationException,\n   removed in JUnit Platform 6); with the 5.x line it instead discovers ZERO\n   tests and reports BUILD SUCCESS — a green build verifying nothing, which is\n   the more dangerous failure.\n\n   Fixed by pinning surefire 3.5.4 locally. junit-jupiter is also moved from\n   6.1.3 to 5.14.2: 6.x needs a Platform the parent''s own surefire cannot\n   load, and nothing here needs JUnit 6. Note surefire.plugin.version reads\n   2.22.2 in BOTH parents and is misleading — the build-section declaration\n   is what applies.\n\n3. OSGi import range narrows, breaking resolution on older Jahia. The parent\n   brings commons-fileupload 1.6, and bnd derives Import-Package ranges from\n   the build classpath, so the import narrowed from [1.3,2) (as shipped in\n   1.0.4) to [1.6,2). That is a resolution requirement: the module would\n   refuse to start on any Jahia exporting an older 1.x.\n\n   Fixed by pinning the range back to [1.3,2) via a bundle-plugin\n   Import-Package instruction. The only API used is\n   ServletFileUpload.isMultipartContent(), unchanged across 1.x, so the\n   narrowing was a build-classpath artifact, not a real requirement.\n\nNet effect on the bundle vs the released 1.0.4: every Import-Package range is\nunchanged except org.jahia.bin.filters and org.jahia.osgi, which gain [8.2,9)\nwhere they previously had no constraint — satisfied by any Jahia 8.2.x.\nBytecode stays at class version 61 (Java 17).\n\ngraphql-dxm-provider is deliberately left at 3.4.0: it is `provided` scope, so\ncompiling against 3.8.1 while a customer runs an older graphql-dxm-provider\nrisks NoSuchMethodError. It keeps its Import-Package range at [3.4,4).\n\nAlso un-ignores the jahia-modules parent in dependabot.yml — tracking the\nbaseline is wanted, and the pom now absorbs what a parent bump breaks — and\nrecords all of the above in AGENTS.md \"Key Facts\", including the\nImport-Package diffing step for future parent bumps.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install, 129 tests (never 0), Java 17 bytecode confirmed,\nImport-Package diffed against the released 1.0.4 jar.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"822d2ded255def1b7be5e47591a6daa713dc85dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/822d2ded255def1b7be5e47591a6daa713dc85dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65","verification":{"payload":"tree 822d2ded255def1b7be5e47591a6daa713dc85dd\nparent 360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786691708 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786691708 +0200\n\nbuild: move to jahia-modules parent 8.2.3.2, absorbing three regressions it introduces\n\nBumps the Jahia platform baseline from 8.2.1.0 to 8.2.3.2 as requested. The\nnew parent breaks the build in three separate ways, each fixed here; two of\nthem fail silently, which is why each has a comment in the pom.\n\n1. Java level silently drops to 11. The parent sets <release>11</release>\n   inside the default-compile and default-testCompile *execution*\n   configurations, and execution-level config beats the\n   maven.compiler.release/source/target properties this pom already set — so\n   those properties were simply ignored and compilation failed on the\n   pattern-matching instanceof in ClamavFilter.sendError.\n\n   Fixed by overriding the same two execution ids. Only <release> is\n   restated, so Maven''s per-element merge keeps the parent''s\n   annotationProcessorPaths (Lombok). Java 17 is retained deliberately;\n   the bundle is therefore Java 17 bytecode and needs a JDK 17 Jahia.\n\n2. Tests stop running, and the build still passes. The parent declares\n   maven-surefire-plugin 2.22.2 (2019) where 8.2.1.0 declared 3.6.0-M1. With\n   junit-jupiter 6.x the forked JVM dies outright\n   (NoClassDefFoundError: org.junit.platform.commons.util.PreconditionViolationException,\n   removed in JUnit Platform 6); with the 5.x line it instead discovers ZERO\n   tests and reports BUILD SUCCESS — a green build verifying nothing, which is\n   the more dangerous failure.\n\n   Fixed by pinning surefire 3.5.4 locally. junit-jupiter is also moved from\n   6.1.3 to 5.14.2: 6.x needs a Platform the parent''s own surefire cannot\n   load, and nothing here needs JUnit 6. Note surefire.plugin.version reads\n   2.22.2 in BOTH parents and is misleading — the build-section declaration\n   is what applies.\n\n3. OSGi import range narrows, breaking resolution on older Jahia. The parent\n   brings commons-fileupload 1.6, and bnd derives Import-Package ranges from\n   the build classpath, so the import narrowed from [1.3,2) (as shipped in\n   1.0.4) to [1.6,2). That is a resolution requirement: the module would\n   refuse to start on any Jahia exporting an older 1.x.\n\n   Fixed by pinning the range back to [1.3,2) via a bundle-plugin\n   Import-Package instruction. The only API used is\n   ServletFileUpload.isMultipartContent(), unchanged across 1.x, so the\n   narrowing was a build-classpath artifact, not a real requirement.\n\nNet effect on the bundle vs the released 1.0.4: every Import-Package range is\nunchanged except org.jahia.bin.filters and org.jahia.osgi, which gain [8.2,9)\nwhere they previously had no constraint — satisfied by any Jahia 8.2.x.\nBytecode stays at class version 61 (Java 17).\n\ngraphql-dxm-provider is deliberately left at 3.4.0: it is `provided` scope, so\ncompiling against 3.8.1 while a customer runs an older graphql-dxm-provider\nrisks NoSuchMethodError. It keeps its Import-Package range at [3.4,4).\n\nAlso un-ignores the jahia-modules parent in dependabot.yml — tracking the\nbaseline is wanted, and the pom now absorbs what a parent bump breaks — and\nrecords all of the above in AGENTS.md \"Key Facts\", including the\nImport-Package diffing step for future parent bumps.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install, 129 tests (never 0), Java 17 bytecode confirmed,\nImport-Package diffed against the released 1.0.4 jar.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+wHwACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kxAwgAnG/AA0x9To1EaLdhDY0mEd8eZ7jTfwrjDULVyzyPoShwRrFsShKHKsRF\nAEk9lcIgD28UzlSzexEhQdjhY2q+LNyJfc35pgo3aiUHWlAFvTnampNMcA7XqDV8\n64ozKsJCLgfcpK115ETbI65qrVTS3XEVL3n0xdtdx3GYUnOG5sTPQ5mcelPFGkql\n77Oj2Q8H5Ggv5vmoqMtoJfaMtmKtqo84AmG4uIjjqYwM+0y1MNbsQopP/I32KG8S\nPGFDnikz5f3vuKlTtr29r5cyex++m77du+yrKiRxafgNPTfnI4+peLK5Ey8jG6zF\nMS1Ev1eKEbRk7GwUIc2gSBW8PS5NJg==\n=iQfp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:16:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDRkNDAyZGQ0NjUxZGY3NjgyM2ZiYWNmZDY4MDllM2QwMmI4MWFiNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2","sha":"360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2"}],"sha":"4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4d402dd4651df76823fbacfd6809e3d02b81ab65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:57:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:57:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"chore(lint): reconcile Prettier with ESLint in the Cypress workspace\n\ntests/.prettierrc.js set `semi: false` while tests/.eslintrc.json extends\n@jahia, which requires semicolons and `object-curly-spacing: never`, and\nnever extended eslint-config-prettier — even though both\neslint-config-prettier and eslint-plugin-prettier were already in\ndevDependencies. The two tools therefore contradicted each other: running\nPrettier on any file here produced code ESLint then rejected (54 errors on\n02-clamavFilter-Permissions.cy.ts alone), and running eslint --fix undid\nit again.\n\nAdds `plugin:prettier/recommended` last in the extends array, so\neslint-config-prettier switches off the conflicting @jahia stylistic rules\nand eslint-plugin-prettier enforces .prettierrc.js as the single formatting\nauthority. Must stay last to win over @jahia.\n\nReformats all five .ts files accordingly. `yarn lint` now enforces\nformatting instead of fighting it, and `yarn lint:fix` repairs drift.\n\nFormatting only — no behavioural change, and the e2e suite is unaffected.\nVerified: eslint exits 0 across tests/.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e352e76c603173db83d7cce106af0ae9ab3a91ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/e352e76c603173db83d7cce106af0ae9ab3a91ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2","verification":{"payload":"tree e352e76c603173db83d7cce106af0ae9ab3a91ba\nparent 7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786690630 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786690630 +0200\n\nchore(lint): reconcile Prettier with ESLint in the Cypress workspace\n\ntests/.prettierrc.js set `semi: false` while tests/.eslintrc.json extends\n@jahia, which requires semicolons and `object-curly-spacing: never`, and\nnever extended eslint-config-prettier — even though both\neslint-config-prettier and eslint-plugin-prettier were already in\ndevDependencies. The two tools therefore contradicted each other: running\nPrettier on any file here produced code ESLint then rejected (54 errors on\n02-clamavFilter-Permissions.cy.ts alone), and running eslint --fix undid\nit again.\n\nAdds `plugin:prettier/recommended` last in the extends array, so\neslint-config-prettier switches off the conflicting @jahia stylistic rules\nand eslint-plugin-prettier enforces .prettierrc.js as the single formatting\nauthority. Must stay last to win over @jahia.\n\nReformats all five .ts files accordingly. `yarn lint` now enforces\nformatting instead of fighting it, and `yarn lint:fix` repairs drift.\n\nFormatting only — no behavioural change, and the e2e suite is unaffected.\nVerified: eslint exits 0 across tests/.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+vEYACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kWPwgArEWqLcSjP2USP0muTVXfn1yKgx9KtExqfvssaPJJ6VHIoYeuvR9lpCgr\nkOii35pSdcOJyjXBqvEWS1ISZrv37gf/f2xPd+1rI8ix/nLO1HsFauWuM/zPRNoF\nooA/6eXYDXWXibIaCMKTI1rBrwo2m4bSoRz5snkurIyvDUtY9/52zI6vTx8HJQJw\nNbZRqAEFjbncNT+DF6KPLG+ozey8/dq+v4+Ur4/IrMMjCzF2LgxYScraJupeq5wx\nUsER00sbTH8moGOQNinaLPQdVI5reZz8ratsINZFqiHj03jIdqsk28bCXxcjdOAQ\npy5Z2XyDStmsCavGAxHRjYFH7izyWw==\n=H0mn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:16:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDM2MGY2NGFjZTM4OTRkZjNhNmM0NTk3NWY2NjAyYzliNTZjZDJhZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8","sha":"7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8"}],"sha":"360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/360f64ace3894df3a6c45975f6602c9b56cd2ae2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:50:53Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:50:53Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"build(deps): stop Dependabot proposing platform-coupled and MF-shared bumps\n\nThe triage in #46 held back four bumps for reasons that will recur every\ntime a new version ships, so encode them in config rather than re-closing\nthe same PRs each week.\n\nModule Federation shared singletons (graphql, @jahia/moonstone,\n@jahia/ui-extender, @apollo/client, react, react-dom): webpack.config.js\nfeeds package.json to getModuleFederationConfig, so each declared range\nbecomes a runtime requirement against whatever the Jahia app-shell\nprovides. A webpack build cannot detect a mismatch — it only surfaces at\nruntime in Jahia — so these track the target Jahia version.\n\nPlatform baseline (org.jahia.modules:jahia-modules parent,\ngraphql-dxm-provider): these define which Jahia release the module\ntargets. graphql-dxm-provider is `provided` scope, so compiling against a\nnewer API than the customer''s runtime risks NoSuchMethodError on their\ninstance.\n\n@babel/core: cannot move to 8 alone — @babel/preset-env,\n@babel/preset-react and babel-jest all peer-depend on ^7, and the\nresolutions entry pins ^7.29.6.\n\nScoping note: the npm entries ignore only semver-major, because an\n`ignore` rule suppresses security updates as well as version updates, and\na CVE fix normally lands as minor/patch inside the current major — those\nstill come through. The two maven entries are ignored outright: both are\nbuild/provided scope, absent from the shipped bundle, and must change only\nas a deliberate decision about the supported Jahia floor.\n\nValidated: dependabot.yml parses and every ignore entry resolves.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0e318668386cebeec4a486e782e193099cdb5ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/f0e318668386cebeec4a486e782e193099cdb5ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8","verification":{"payload":"tree f0e318668386cebeec4a486e782e193099cdb5ec\nparent 4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786690253 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786690253 +0200\n\nbuild(deps): stop Dependabot proposing platform-coupled and MF-shared bumps\n\nThe triage in #46 held back four bumps for reasons that will recur every\ntime a new version ships, so encode them in config rather than re-closing\nthe same PRs each week.\n\nModule Federation shared singletons (graphql, @jahia/moonstone,\n@jahia/ui-extender, @apollo/client, react, react-dom): webpack.config.js\nfeeds package.json to getModuleFederationConfig, so each declared range\nbecomes a runtime requirement against whatever the Jahia app-shell\nprovides. A webpack build cannot detect a mismatch — it only surfaces at\nruntime in Jahia — so these track the target Jahia version.\n\nPlatform baseline (org.jahia.modules:jahia-modules parent,\ngraphql-dxm-provider): these define which Jahia release the module\ntargets. graphql-dxm-provider is `provided` scope, so compiling against a\nnewer API than the customer''s runtime risks NoSuchMethodError on their\ninstance.\n\n@babel/core: cannot move to 8 alone — @babel/preset-env,\n@babel/preset-react and babel-jest all peer-depend on ^7, and the\nresolutions entry pins ^7.29.6.\n\nScoping note: the npm entries ignore only semver-major, because an\n`ignore` rule suppresses security updates as well as version updates, and\na CVE fix normally lands as minor/patch inside the current major — those\nstill come through. The two maven entries are ignored outright: both are\nbuild/provided scope, absent from the shipped bundle, and must change only\nas a deliberate decision about the supported Jahia floor.\n\nValidated: dependabot.yml parses and every ignore entry resolves.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+us0ACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3kv7Af/WL3YeOwB6ncKu1+yyGxKTb37LhV2+L3BjuKk3SZBKWeqj/ncnU+CQe+k\nsWun+Z5WsuYm2hI4osZPGsyH4AW8iBdg5uxEXQZHges4c4PuEmXRClahMWy9T72b\n8BoxhDL2p+mFNmUsyc54tZJE6QVTPnVP749OaDf1xMmNNd9dlcbkqw7cxnFSso/i\nXFXdeB4tMMT1fm+uEpW5ctSFInbfjGsIxH/v3hpsIHkILbb2+OUR/IX38GCQmkZg\nOx7u3yL0n3Z1PEgqSM6WPwBC93zSrq0aU3XR7onZc502yeFB26xdO2yPFPcUgtOX\n/OWwaoh/jTYcvpS1ug2FaptgMTRjpw==\n=DbMJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:50:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDdlNmM0NTMyMTk0ZTA4ZDM0ZTAwNzI0N2VkZThkNTE2N2JiOWYzZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359","sha":"4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359"}],"sha":"7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/7e6c4532194e08d34e007247ede8d5167bb9f3e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:48:18Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:48:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build(deps): accept build- and test-scoped Dependabot updates, hold platform-coupled ones (#46)\n\nConsolidates the 13 Dependabot PRs opened once .github/dependabot.yml was\nrepaired and version updates ran for the first time. They all share the two\nyarn.lock files or pom.xml, so merging them individually would conflict\npairwise; each accepted bump below was applied and verified together.\n\nAccepted — build- and test-scope only, no effect on the shipped bundle:\n\n  pom.xml     junit-jupiter            5.10.2  -> 6.1.3    (test)\n  pom.xml     mockito-core             5.14.2  -> 5.23.0   (test)\n  pom.xml     logback-classic          1.4.14  -> 1.6.2    (test)\n  pom.xml     frontend-maven-plugin    1.15.0  -> 2.0.2    (build)\n  root        @jahia/eslint-config     2.1.0   -> 2.2.0\n  root        @testing-library/user-event ^14.5.0 -> ^14.6.3\n  root        sass                     ^1.52.1 -> ^1.102.0\n  root        webpack                  ^5.91.0 -> ^5.109.2\n  root        webpack-cli              ^5.1.4  -> ^7.2.2\n  root        webpack-bundle-analyzer  ^4.10.2 -> ^5.3.1\n  tests       cypress                  15.13.1 -> 15.20.1\n  tests       webpack                  5.104.1 -> 5.109.2\n  tests       eslint-plugin-jest       ^27.2.1 -> ^29.16.0\n  tests       eslint-plugin-react-hooks ^4.6.0 -> ^7.1.1\n  tests       mocha                    ^10.0.0 -> ^11.8.0\n\nBonus: cypress 15.20.1 drops extract-zip entirely, so GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv\nis now fixed by removal rather than tolerated. That alert had been dismissed\nas unfixable because the latest published extract-zip was the vulnerable\n2.0.1 and cypress pinned it exactly.\n\nHeld back deliberately — these are not routine dependency bumps:\n\n  parent jahia-modules 8.2.1.0 -> 8.2.3.2 (#32) and\n  graphql-dxm-provider 3.4.0 -> 3.8.1 (#32, provided scope)\n    Both move the Jahia platform baseline. 1.0.4 was just released against\n    8.2.1.0, and compiling against a newer provided API than the target\n    runtime risks NoSuchMethodError on customer instances. Needs a\n    deliberate decision about the supported Jahia floor, not a dep bump.\n\n  @jahia/moonstone ^2.16.2 -> ^2.20.3 (#38) and\n  graphql ^15.8.0 -> ^16.14.2 (#44)\n    Both are Module Federation shared singletons: webpack.config.js feeds\n    package.json to getModuleFederationConfig, so the declared range becomes\n    a runtime requirement against whatever the Jahia app-shell provides.\n    Raising them demands an app-shell that supplies the newer version, and a\n    webpack build cannot detect the mismatch — it only surfaces at runtime.\n    These must track the target Jahia version.\n\n  @babel/core ^7.x -> ^8.0.1 (#41 root, #39 tests)\n    Incoherent as a lone bump: @babel/preset-env, @babel/preset-react and\n    babel-jest all peer-depend on @babel/core ^7, and the resolutions entry\n    pins ^7.29.6. Babel 8 needs all of those moved together.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (129 tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint\nin both workspaces, yarn build:production, cypress 15.20.1 binary verifies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbb262f908ddda5f43868644a745ee800e4aa477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/bbb262f908ddda5f43868644a745ee800e4aa477"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359","verification":{"payload":"tree bbb262f908ddda5f43868644a745ee800e4aa477\nparent 32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786690098 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786690098 +0200\n\nbuild(deps): accept build- and test-scoped Dependabot updates, hold platform-coupled ones (#46)\n\nConsolidates the 13 Dependabot PRs opened once .github/dependabot.yml was\nrepaired and version updates ran for the first time. They all share the two\nyarn.lock files or pom.xml, so merging them individually would conflict\npairwise; each accepted bump below was applied and verified together.\n\nAccepted — build- and test-scope only, no effect on the shipped bundle:\n\n  pom.xml     junit-jupiter            5.10.2  -> 6.1.3    (test)\n  pom.xml     mockito-core             5.14.2  -> 5.23.0   (test)\n  pom.xml     logback-classic          1.4.14  -> 1.6.2    (test)\n  pom.xml     frontend-maven-plugin    1.15.0  -> 2.0.2    (build)\n  root        @jahia/eslint-config     2.1.0   -> 2.2.0\n  root        @testing-library/user-event ^14.5.0 -> ^14.6.3\n  root        sass                     ^1.52.1 -> ^1.102.0\n  root        webpack                  ^5.91.0 -> ^5.109.2\n  root        webpack-cli              ^5.1.4  -> ^7.2.2\n  root        webpack-bundle-analyzer  ^4.10.2 -> ^5.3.1\n  tests       cypress                  15.13.1 -> 15.20.1\n  tests       webpack                  5.104.1 -> 5.109.2\n  tests       eslint-plugin-jest       ^27.2.1 -> ^29.16.0\n  tests       eslint-plugin-react-hooks ^4.6.0 -> ^7.1.1\n  tests       mocha                    ^10.0.0 -> ^11.8.0\n\nBonus: cypress 15.20.1 drops extract-zip entirely, so GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv\nis now fixed by removal rather than tolerated. That alert had been dismissed\nas unfixable because the latest published extract-zip was the vulnerable\n2.0.1 and cypress pinned it exactly.\n\nHeld back deliberately — these are not routine dependency bumps:\n\n  parent jahia-modules 8.2.1.0 -> 8.2.3.2 (#32) and\n  graphql-dxm-provider 3.4.0 -> 3.8.1 (#32, provided scope)\n    Both move the Jahia platform baseline. 1.0.4 was just released against\n    8.2.1.0, and compiling against a newer provided API than the target\n    runtime risks NoSuchMethodError on customer instances. Needs a\n    deliberate decision about the supported Jahia floor, not a dep bump.\n\n  @jahia/moonstone ^2.16.2 -> ^2.20.3 (#38) and\n  graphql ^15.8.0 -> ^16.14.2 (#44)\n    Both are Module Federation shared singletons: webpack.config.js feeds\n    package.json to getModuleFederationConfig, so the declared range becomes\n    a runtime requirement against whatever the Jahia app-shell provides.\n    Raising them demands an app-shell that supplies the newer version, and a\n    webpack build cannot detect the mismatch — it only surfaces at runtime.\n    These must track the target Jahia version.\n\n  @babel/core ^7.x -> ^8.0.1 (#41 root, #39 tests)\n    Incoherent as a lone bump: @babel/preset-env, @babel/preset-react and\n    babel-jest all peer-depend on @babel/core ^7, and the resolutions entry\n    pins ^7.29.6. Babel 8 needs all of those moved together.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (129 tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint\nin both workspaces, yarn build:production, cypress 15.20.1 binary verifies.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfroyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3PYQAIvKDDhM3ZuJ0Kfy/Ajgny86\nUSFqwbuxObf/kTA/DYj44wFEvqM3wDj+Mxvp4NQCtBL8l9igE+kQ3uqbMjLK1/at\nLKWUWgiR2MGTwXy2VfA+4TLQXG/OixYGQN8uvItaEAUladwnL/I4PLrfuBVp9YAh\n0M2aELOkX6YYh72mVTZ910eW5tsaz5gOPq9WcUWgauf0j0b4ccheJEmdbeFdCIN8\n92zSSCLnRNkuh6XEsC1swwvTMioVZFNu8mfJm6+yX/SV6W7rNpVGUJZCYGOn4F/1\n8zhMGLHbGmmaQTE7q2PYYR8Mkv0UJ6MyrRP4tTBFm4M6uFmddFFyZ0oJFCjBWaTf\nThX18U6E4ze4g0EVKryy7t9xk/IausNTiNtRRPf+DTT4S9IYjCVDVQARUgrNZqRj\nJYPxZev5P0TCIvIOLVWsMm4UGNpHJ/mVbsSreVcbD8pE3dwzsGMfO2hJTNNpkZm0\nB/PBESkQHAlQsKpJKCaW5u/TCzx6yz54JVuysIC1IoWmQjxR/n8gq1OR0sRqWqoN\nHI5biuTaCJ02N0rR3xuz+xshfBbYQmPWBk/JX+Z/l2IZFI6hJAgVNARVvfLER0I8\nKbF6pxGy25B6CGYEuKjLC9hWouw3k3baRL0Zaqg0ZUbtnq/oTIsUwc9wweJdUopS\n2cmz4SxFAHZa3cObh5uM\n=JxHk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:48:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDRhMTIwMjRhYTYwMmMyMjE0NWY5YjExZTMzMGI2NGUxNTlmM2EzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c","sha":"32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c"}],"sha":"4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/4a12024aa602c22145f9b11e330b64e159f3a359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:39:24Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:39:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: post-1.0.4 cleanup — AGENTS.md GraphQL accuracy + six code findings (#45)\n\n* docs: correct AGENTS.md GraphQL API to the namespaced schema\n\nThe GraphQL table still documented the flat root fields (clamavSettings,\nclamavPing, clamavScanTest, clamavSaveSettings) that f56a5d8 replaced\nwith a single `clamav` namespace container. Those field names no longer\nexist in the schema — 04-clamavFilter-SchemaNamespace.cy.ts asserts their\nabsence — so the primary developer reference described an API that would\nfail against the running module.\n\nUpdates the table to the nested paths, adds an example query and the\nJava-side extension/return-type mapping, and fixes the two Gotchas\nentries plus the validation heading that used the old names.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: resolve six code-analysis findings in the ClamAV core\n\nNo behavioural change except the ManagedService delete contract, noted below.\n\n1. Remove dead Forms-specific upload detection. `isFormsOctetStreamUpload`\n   was superseded by `isRawBinaryUpload` in SEC-141 (e1bd893), which\n   matches any application/octet-stream body regardless of path. The\n   one-arg private overload had no callers at all; the two-arg overload\n   and FORMS_UPLOAD_PATH were reachable only from tests (Sonar S1144).\n   Dropped both overloads, the constant and its five tests — those tests\n   only exercised dead code, while isRawBinaryUpload''s own six tests\n   cover the live behaviour including the Forms path.\n\n2. ClamavQuery returned the literal \"CONNECTION_FAILED\" while\n   Status.CONNECTION_FAILED existed — precisely the drift the adjacent\n   comment guards against for Status.ERROR. Now derived from the enum.\n\n3. ClamavServiceImpl.clamavConfig is now volatile. It is written by the\n   OSGi DS bind thread and read by concurrent request threads through\n   scan()/ping(), the same situation ClamavFilter.clamavService already\n   documents and guards.\n\n4. ClamavConfig.updated(null) now reverts to the compiled-in defaults.\n   Per the ManagedService contract a null dictionary means the\n   configuration was deleted; retaining the last-known values left a\n   deleted .cfg silently in force, so an operator seeing no configuration\n   still had the module pointing at the old host. This is the one\n   behavioural change here.\n\n   The pre-existing test could not catch it — it called updated(null) on a\n   fresh instance, where no-op and revert are indistinguishable. Added a\n   test that configures the instance first; verified it fails against the\n   old code (expected \"localhost\", got \"clamav.custom\") and passes now.\n\n5. sanitize() compiled its regex on every call, on a logging path. Now a\n   precompiled static Pattern.\n\n6. The raw-binary scan path logged \"Forms upload scan\", stale since it\n   stopped being Forms-specific. Renamed scanOctetStream to scanRawBinary\n   and corrected the message.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install, 129 tests pass (133 - 5 dead-code tests + 1\nnew regression guard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"72f1ae0724318dc46fe126d6e4d899028bc27127","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/72f1ae0724318dc46fe126d6e4d899028bc27127"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c","verification":{"payload":"tree 72f1ae0724318dc46fe126d6e4d899028bc27127\nparent 5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786689564 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786689564 +0200\n\nchore: post-1.0.4 cleanup — AGENTS.md GraphQL accuracy + six code findings (#45)\n\n* docs: correct AGENTS.md GraphQL API to the namespaced schema\n\nThe GraphQL table still documented the flat root fields (clamavSettings,\nclamavPing, clamavScanTest, clamavSaveSettings) that f56a5d8 replaced\nwith a single `clamav` namespace container. Those field names no longer\nexist in the schema — 04-clamavFilter-SchemaNamespace.cy.ts asserts their\nabsence — so the primary developer reference described an API that would\nfail against the running module.\n\nUpdates the table to the nested paths, adds an example query and the\nJava-side extension/return-type mapping, and fixes the two Gotchas\nentries plus the validation heading that used the old names.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: resolve six code-analysis findings in the ClamAV core\n\nNo behavioural change except the ManagedService delete contract, noted below.\n\n1. Remove dead Forms-specific upload detection. `isFormsOctetStreamUpload`\n   was superseded by `isRawBinaryUpload` in SEC-141 (e1bd893), which\n   matches any application/octet-stream body regardless of path. The\n   one-arg private overload had no callers at all; the two-arg overload\n   and FORMS_UPLOAD_PATH were reachable only from tests (Sonar S1144).\n   Dropped both overloads, the constant and its five tests — those tests\n   only exercised dead code, while isRawBinaryUpload''s own six tests\n   cover the live behaviour including the Forms path.\n\n2. ClamavQuery returned the literal \"CONNECTION_FAILED\" while\n   Status.CONNECTION_FAILED existed — precisely the drift the adjacent\n   comment guards against for Status.ERROR. Now derived from the enum.\n\n3. ClamavServiceImpl.clamavConfig is now volatile. It is written by the\n   OSGi DS bind thread and read by concurrent request threads through\n   scan()/ping(), the same situation ClamavFilter.clamavService already\n   documents and guards.\n\n4. ClamavConfig.updated(null) now reverts to the compiled-in defaults.\n   Per the ManagedService contract a null dictionary means the\n   configuration was deleted; retaining the last-known values left a\n   deleted .cfg silently in force, so an operator seeing no configuration\n   still had the module pointing at the old host. This is the one\n   behavioural change here.\n\n   The pre-existing test could not catch it — it called updated(null) on a\n   fresh instance, where no-op and revert are indistinguishable. Added a\n   test that configures the instance first; verified it fails against the\n   old code (expected \"localhost\", got \"clamav.custom\") and passes now.\n\n5. sanitize() compiled its regex on every call, on a logging path. Now a\n   precompiled static Pattern.\n\n6. The raw-binary scan path logged \"Forms upload scan\", stale since it\n   stopped being Forms-specific. Renamed scanOctetStream to scanRawBinary\n   and corrected the message.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install, 129 tests pass (133 - 5 dead-code tests + 1\nnew regression guard).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrgcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4RsQAH4qS+ECTsAjCxyEHtJhHxXz\n2dhXKiH3UGaAZeTcJ0udtCb1r1vGJgIN2buDCHrmqLXJW/hQFViUr1RypRvKSSBZ\n8pQlbZuPpi0iu+HMjJUdwdqknLnSASJHlAfEzgwO7NkOG0FKQv+2FFfeh5YcTsu4\ntfIxby69cxl2glxv3q21YPo5ED5Bq9uPYIKbSmMSO17JbtVWURsDL2zvPGWfdujZ\n0VLswoXfXnF6aHjvtVBLD8nTek2lIewtefjnuC1ui0nJJflc3xGd50+T25xM6/o6\nVImX2uvwKZsnrV1TFOGHELwWHLahH6n/2gAvFd84PcNIY1DQhF2F1JEOVi3CK/D2\nroPjZNEwGRL7SKnA580W34r9tOSRCRAcRRSurB2b5JvoudeQSD090NuI0SW+rN0k\nE1icrcC2JHci9gFfitYwSaW2s/+UkEdfcyaBeKPV1KnnkNJE5H6LkA/w5wp1ldFL\nkINl4T5+67ONxGcaHxj1u0+O6nVs0XbITWulPbMWuw7LuVoCcu1y26L+pEmizkQV\n2JvRnKjA1qtcKOLalyvE6e39iEbCqEpnSElREjBwIIbTYkLEahK5gczNBDjuw+es\nt46pxEnjt9gObrZo1vTeSmQz1GPcZFiM1u2EfL47+LaJD+tLgL8k6MHR3A1Zdkii\nEesk2wKi7zbaZsfrbmx4\n=w/+3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:44:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDMyZmRlNmUwODUwNzJjZTdjZGZjZDQxMmM3MTA2OTVkMmJkZDk3NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200","sha":"5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200"}],"sha":"32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/32fde6e085072ce7cdfcd412c710695d2bdd975c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:19:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:19:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix(deps): refresh brace-expansion 2.x to 2.1.4 for GHSA advisory\n\nA new advisory covering brace-expansion >=2.0.0 <2.1.2 was published\nafter 1.0.4 was tagged. The root lockfile held the 2.x line at 2.1.0.\n\nThe earlier sweep deliberately left this line alone: at that time the\nopen advisories covered only <1.1.16 and >=3.0.0 <5.0.7, and the 2.x\nentry was not flagged.\n\nThe declared `^2.0.2` range already permits the patched release, so\nre-resolving is sufficient — no `resolutions` entry needed, and a global\none would be wrong here anyway since three brace-expansion major lines\ncoexist in this tree (^1.1.7, ^2.0.2, ^5.0.5).\n\nBuild-time transitive dependency only; absent from the OSGi bundle, so\nthe released 1.0.4 artifact is unaffected.\n\nVerified: yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint, webpack build.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fbe160151d4de8ef6a93621ef5c95323d8f9175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/4fbe160151d4de8ef6a93621ef5c95323d8f9175"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fbe160151d4de8ef6a93621ef5c95323d8f9175\nparent 2cd36a11f9faf4eccf1ce55ea3d1dc2d0aaec8c6\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786688375 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786688375 +0200\n\nfix(deps): refresh brace-expansion 2.x to 2.1.4 for GHSA advisory\n\nA new advisory covering brace-expansion >=2.0.0 <2.1.2 was published\nafter 1.0.4 was tagged. The root lockfile held the 2.x line at 2.1.0.\n\nThe earlier sweep deliberately left this line alone: at that time the\nopen advisories covered only <1.1.16 and >=3.0.0 <5.0.7, and the 2.x\nentry was not flagged.\n\nThe declared `^2.0.2` range already permits the patched release, so\nre-resolving is sufficient — no `resolutions` entry needed, and a global\none would be wrong here anyway since three brace-expansion major lines\ncoexist in this tree (^1.1.7, ^2.0.2, ^5.0.5).\n\nBuild-time transitive dependency only; absent from the OSGi bundle, so\nthe released 1.0.4 artifact is unaffected.\n\nVerified: yarn test (36 Jest tests), yarn lint, webpack build.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+s3cACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n9qAgArSLy7wJYAwFea3i4ddIJ+yswOPmBpFujkHWKV/MdtQcgwF/Zw7bPXDYB\nyb3q7vNB5tSFdGkChpgynkL9GhNeRuiIV+p2cO6z5VBGWwpbBR0x/iwnkRaFIVMk\ndaB/2vG85SUq5uvhFrhOScMNnudzQxfPw3O72QI4Ob/P1QG2MsZwjJQVufZ/xNIq\nMo0YQg/zklTp1fX0VuT0BBEwTCju5FCBRUYIPGxlfoKGlSft0bbb80qKPobWCpzW\nb73tYDznCWslmgpgX2nfwvLZA7oWbWellc3sIomMb1RPZsqYajICfiEtTYV92dnF\ns+Xe1QIG19PiCD4gWFtAPKR2VjkrTw==\n=rF0m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:20:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/5cbe723989cea478ce5d68281d3135249d3f1200","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDVjYmU3MjM5ODljZWE0NzhjZTVkNjgyODFkMzEzNTI0OWQzZjEyM