"url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/457d0b65dace8f2025e06fee0b873305be764600","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDQ1N2QwYjY1ZGFjZThmMjAyNWUwNmZlZTBiODczMzA1YmU3NjQ2MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f","sha":"efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f"}],"sha":"457d0b65dace8f2025e06fee0b873305be764600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/457d0b65dace8f2025e06fee0b873305be764600"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:15:14Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:15:14Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"docs: correct upload-coverage claims stale since SEC-141\n\nThe README''s \"How it works\" and \"Security considerations → Upload\ncoverage\" sections still described the pre-SEC-141 behaviour, stating\nthat only multipart/form-data and the Forms octet-stream endpoint are\nscanned and that WebDAV PUT and raw-body JCR REST uploads are \"not\nintercepted by this filter; defend those separately\".\n\nThat is the opposite of what the code has done since e1bd893.\nClamavFilter.isRawBinaryUpload() scans any application/octet-stream body\nand any PUT carrying a body, so WebDAV and raw JCR-REST binary writes\nare covered.\n\nUnderstating coverage in a security module''s own documentation is\nactively harmful: an operator reading it would either build compensating\ncontrols that are no longer needed, or distrust protection they already\nhave. Corrected in README.md and in the two matching AGENTS.md spots so\nthe docs do not contradict each other.\n\nAlso notes that multipart scanning covers every part, including multiple\nfiles posted under the same field name (the getMultiFileMap behaviour),\nand keeps an explicit caveat that ingestion paths which never traverse\nthis servlet filter are still out of scope.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e05a0eb70fd261c043555bb53b408860db277db6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/e05a0eb70fd261c043555bb53b408860db277db6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f","verification":{"payload":"tree e05a0eb70fd261c043555bb53b408860db277db6\nparent c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786688114 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786688114 +0200\n\ndocs: correct upload-coverage claims stale since SEC-141\n\nThe README''s \"How it works\" and \"Security considerations → Upload\ncoverage\" sections still described the pre-SEC-141 behaviour, stating\nthat only multipart/form-data and the Forms octet-stream endpoint are\nscanned and that WebDAV PUT and raw-body JCR REST uploads are \"not\nintercepted by this filter; defend those separately\".\n\nThat is the opposite of what the code has done since e1bd893.\nClamavFilter.isRawBinaryUpload() scans any application/octet-stream body\nand any PUT carrying a body, so WebDAV and raw JCR-REST binary writes\nare covered.\n\nUnderstating coverage in a security module''s own documentation is\nactively harmful: an operator reading it would either build compensating\ncontrols that are no longer needed, or distrust protection they already\nhave. Corrected in README.md and in the two matching AGENTS.md spots so\nthe docs do not contradict each other.\n\nAlso notes that multipart scanning covers every part, including multiple\nfiles posted under the same field name (the getMultiFileMap behaviour),\nand keeps an explicit caveat that ingestion paths which never traverse\nthis servlet filter are still out of scope.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmp+snIACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3lyWAf8D7s1A9YfujjMHYHMSnISHd7YzRqBdmfhQJXTPHx0V4EPhBPxLdboIh1v\niuyexO2OZHDvFdXHZSM6SkpFH6NwV2ulVF6Ma78MXF0M+Vg1ueBtPLK63GU8egVE\nE2FKEQEczXSC7pEgzJ8dSxtsGz8CAqO5uhEtXzbB7ALq+oNG+PY8nuKEaGF9avgh\nBmjuTENVWdUwfTqqPBdrufKwuiQtwP5MRxM0V22cqvvyUXybKnLnND+10F3cnhE3\n2LGTeGLtL/uYp7RWn6QD7gHIF6XTjJlglB89BTLHGIPCWV0eSo3x0oCSXqvvO9zI\nydBAmv1Njfe5Y2g5dpckZrFoNa8xAw==\n=cy+v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:15:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGVmYTUyN2IyYTJhOTI2YzE1OTFhNzM5YzNmMjhkMjcwYzViZTgyNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b","sha":"c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b"}],"sha":"efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/efa527b2a2a926c1591a739c3f28d270c5be824f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:13:11Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:13:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): resolve all patchable Dependabot alerts in both Yarn workspaces (#31)\n\nCloses 26 of the 27 open Dependabot alerts across yarn.lock and\ntests/yarn.lock. All affected packages are build-time/dev transitive\ndependencies; none ship inside the OSGi bundle.\n\nMost alerts were a stale lockfile rather than a missing release: the\ndeclared range already permitted the patched version, so re-resolving is\nenough and is durable (Yarn always picks the highest satisfying version):\n\n  root      brace-expansion  1.1.14 -> 1.1.18   (GHSA, <1.1.16)\n  root      brace-expansion  5.0.6  -> 5.0.9    (>=3.0.0 <5.0.7)\n  root      postcss          8.5.14 -> 8.5.26   (<=8.5.22)\n  root      immutable        5.1.5  -> 5.1.9    (<5.1.8)\n  root      ws               7.5.10 -> 7.5.13   (>=7.0.0 <7.5.11)\n  tests     js-yaml          3.15.0 -> 3.15.1   (>=3.0.0 <3.15.1)\n  tests     js-yaml          4.3.0  -> 4.3.1    (>=4.0.0 <4.3.1)\n\nStale `resolutions` floors were raised so the patched version is a hard\nrequirement rather than a lockfile coincidence:\n\n  both      fast-uri    ^3.1.2  -> ^3.1.5   (3.1.5)\n  both      ip-address  ^10.1.1 -> ^10.4.0  (10.5.0)\n  both      tar         ^7.5.16 -> ^7.5.22  (7.5.22)\n  root      js-yaml     ^4.1.1  -> ^4.3.1   (4.3.1)\n\nTwo alerts could not be reached by re-resolution because the declared\nrange structurally excludes the fix, so they needed new resolutions:\n\n  tests     qs    ~6.14.1 -> ^6.15.3  (6.15.2 is outside ~6.14.1)\n  tests     uuid  ^8.3.2  -> ^11.1.1  (patched only in 11.1.1)\n\nThe uuid bump crosses majors. Its three consumers (@cypress/request,\nmochawesome, jahia-reporter) only ever call v4(), whose signature is\nunchanged, and uuid 11 still exposes a CJS `require` entry; both\nconsumers were verified to require() and generate ids successfully. The\nadvisory itself (missing bounds check when an explicit `buf` is passed)\nis unreachable for v4()-only callers.\n\nextract-zip (GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv) is left open deliberately: latest\npublished is still the vulnerable 2.0.1 and Cypress pins it exactly, so\nno fix exists to apply.\n\nLockfiles were regenerated with Yarn 1.22.22 to match the yarnVersion\npinned in frontend-maven-plugin; a subsequent `mvn install` left both\nbyte-identical.\n\nAlso fixes the broken .github/dependabot.yml, which shipped as the\nGitHub scaffold with an invalid empty `package-ecosystem` — no version\nupdates ever ran, so routine patches only ever surfaced later as\nungrouped security alerts. Now configures npm (/ and /tests) plus maven,\nwith grouped updates to stop the one-PR-per-alert churn.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (133 Java tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests),\nyarn lint in both workspaces, webpack production build.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"82cf73c02f4c2f30e991978f9d2b68f589e4a60b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/82cf73c02f4c2f30e991978f9d2b68f589e4a60b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b","verification":{"payload":"tree 82cf73c02f4c2f30e991978f9d2b68f589e4a60b\nparent 8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1786687991 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786687991 +0200\n\nfix(deps): resolve all patchable Dependabot alerts in both Yarn workspaces (#31)\n\nCloses 26 of the 27 open Dependabot alerts across yarn.lock and\ntests/yarn.lock. All affected packages are build-time/dev transitive\ndependencies; none ship inside the OSGi bundle.\n\nMost alerts were a stale lockfile rather than a missing release: the\ndeclared range already permitted the patched version, so re-resolving is\nenough and is durable (Yarn always picks the highest satisfying version):\n\n  root      brace-expansion  1.1.14 -> 1.1.18   (GHSA, <1.1.16)\n  root      brace-expansion  5.0.6  -> 5.0.9    (>=3.0.0 <5.0.7)\n  root      postcss          8.5.14 -> 8.5.26   (<=8.5.22)\n  root      immutable        5.1.5  -> 5.1.9    (<5.1.8)\n  root      ws               7.5.10 -> 7.5.13   (>=7.0.0 <7.5.11)\n  tests     js-yaml          3.15.0 -> 3.15.1   (>=3.0.0 <3.15.1)\n  tests     js-yaml          4.3.0  -> 4.3.1    (>=4.0.0 <4.3.1)\n\nStale `resolutions` floors were raised so the patched version is a hard\nrequirement rather than a lockfile coincidence:\n\n  both      fast-uri    ^3.1.2  -> ^3.1.5   (3.1.5)\n  both      ip-address  ^10.1.1 -> ^10.4.0  (10.5.0)\n  both      tar         ^7.5.16 -> ^7.5.22  (7.5.22)\n  root      js-yaml     ^4.1.1  -> ^4.3.1   (4.3.1)\n\nTwo alerts could not be reached by re-resolution because the declared\nrange structurally excludes the fix, so they needed new resolutions:\n\n  tests     qs    ~6.14.1 -> ^6.15.3  (6.15.2 is outside ~6.14.1)\n  tests     uuid  ^8.3.2  -> ^11.1.1  (patched only in 11.1.1)\n\nThe uuid bump crosses majors. Its three consumers (@cypress/request,\nmochawesome, jahia-reporter) only ever call v4(), whose signature is\nunchanged, and uuid 11 still exposes a CJS `require` entry; both\nconsumers were verified to require() and generate ids successfully. The\nadvisory itself (missing bounds check when an explicit `buf` is passed)\nis unreachable for v4()-only callers.\n\nextract-zip (GHSA-jmr9-qjv8-65gv) is left open deliberately: latest\npublished is still the vulnerable 2.0.1 and Cypress pins it exactly, so\nno fix exists to apply.\n\nLockfiles were regenerated with Yarn 1.22.22 to match the yarnVersion\npinned in frontend-maven-plugin; a subsequent `mvn install` left both\nbyte-identical.\n\nAlso fixes the broken .github/dependabot.yml, which shipped as the\nGitHub scaffold with an invalid empty `package-ecosystem` — no version\nupdates ever ran, so routine patches only ever surfaced later as\nungrouped security alerts. Now configures npm (/ and /tests) plus maven,\nwith grouped updates to stop the one-PR-per-alert churn.\n\nVerified: mvn clean install (133 Java tests), yarn test (36 Jest tests),\nyarn lint in both workspaces, webpack production build.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrH3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABwAQABy8utP5KtORJL9AgCLH1XRF\nON6tzF0b1gROefnjPNvtOmNvt9jXxBXrzIKU9BnE76Sm8yySPvu2C66PLAShw2xE\nnjWRfXeddZd7taT7KRgUvOyIq7F0UR8RvozDDiphiVDKa7yMzyT8sP2OWL0/14hW\n+oQyAYdPEYPe6S1qHgegD7FZyrlBNqLTerhkTL1oqBHIi5z7kJ5hAQV7xQd/k2Jf\n0N7sXg6lNOgMJ0DokzbIQjIne0xwKoUuJ0W33u+oEc2ZQEQEygqAxexcGJnVVjFL\nsZPyoG4Wu5W5eMr1MLRNDyHb3rcq3wawgeAHtz03wwKSAgeqMUEOee6XEWxzIa6a\nMFXZHY81LR/plCA0q1rv45SA+A9eAWe8WMcG7mO4BHyQPfE7tN0gHCMz/UHqtU09\ni/bkjBsNiJMA14K5drbwtUE2O/CjES/9PA1muHeFxqHG8zYw0mWAYVXPKth5L4ji\njs7wOFjQ4LCS+EP64n6ugB0WDZjdC6P+2RvPCnZqac59MrdH0YeY8t+U2Cs3c9rO\ne7wycFL85DnU3wzGSaiJFwCyOWp0dzIJwQMyfh8E2H4NkTM/8arawkPrbwY/xfnp\n+FJfNPxZ2H/2zvfiVWf/F5ZFbWKNojUAWAp1Tx02/0x3G8JqkRxcCmeI+knegaOH\nna9a/BLP5RtvFttDhVFj\n=TF4N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:14:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKGM0YjlmZWI1ZmI1YWYwZDBjY2I0ZGVkYjg0ZTQwZGM0OGQ1Mzg4OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b","sha":"8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b"}],"sha":"c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/c4b9feb5fb5af0d0ccb4dedb84e40dc48d53888b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:28:01Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:28:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add JUnit/Jest/Cypress coverage for fail-closed core, GraphQL resolvers, and admin UI (SUPPORT-646) (#22)\n\n* test(filter,config): cover isRawBinaryUpload and ClamavConfig gaps (SUPPORT-646 Group 1)\n\n- ClamavFilterTest: add the isRawBinaryUpload() 5-row table test (U1 JUnit half) —\n  previously untested despite being the SEC-141 raw-binary/PUT routing predicate.\n- ClamavConfigTest: fix the F9 downgrade by asserting a second updated() call on\n  the same live instance replaces the first (live-reload semantics), add the\n  previously zero-coverage connection_timeout/read_timeout out-of-range rejection\n  branch with atomicity re-checks, and add a partial-update case proving omitted\n  keys retain their prior (non-default) values rather than resetting to defaults.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 1.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(filter): cover ClamavFilter.doFilter fail-closed core (SUPPORT-646 Group 2)\n\nAdds ClamavFilterDoFilterTest, a new shared harness (real multipart bytes parsed\nby a real CommonsMultipartResolver, plain octet-stream/PUT request builders, a\nstreaming-only zero-filled InputStream for the 100 MiB streaming-cap case) plus\n26 tests covering doFilter() end to end, which had zero direct test coverage\nbefore this change despite being the security-critical fail-closed core:\n\n- F1/F3: happy-path forwarding of the WRAPPED request to the chain, with\n  byte-identity proof between what was scanned and the original file content.\n- F2: an attacker-controlled parameter/header has zero effect on whether\n  scanning occurs.\n- F4: both oversize entry paths (declared Content-Length pre-check and the\n  streaming RequestTooLargeException catch) return 413.\n- F5: infected uploads return 403 and the log line is pinned to exactly\n  \"Uploaded file is a malware\" (and asserted to NOT contain the signature,\n  documenting today''s actual, doc-divergent behavior per Stage 2).\n- F6: all four fail-closed scenarios (service never bound, ping()==false,\n  scan()->Status.ERROR), for both the multipart and octet-stream entry paths,\n  with an explicit assertion that scan() is never invoked once ping() has\n  failed (pins the `service == null || !service.ping()` short-circuit order).\n- F7: a genuine MalformedStreamException from a truncated multipart body, and\n  a stream IOException, both resolve to 500.\n- D4: a 12-row parameterized umbrella asserting chain.doFilter() is NEVER\n  invoked across every non-clean outcome enumerated above plus both oversize\n  paths — the single highest-value regression guard in this set, since it\n  generalizes beyond any individually enumerated scenario.\n\nAdds ch.qos.logback:logback-classic as a test-only dependency: the module has\nno SLF4J provider on the unit-test classpath otherwise (it relies on the OSGi\ncontainer''s own logging backend at runtime), so a real Logger implementation is\nneeded to attach a ListAppender for the F5/F7 log-content assertions.\n\nAll 26 new tests pass against the current, unmodified ClamavFilter — the\nfail-closed guarantee held up under from-scratch, adversarial test-writing\nscrutiny; no gap was found in the security-critical core itself.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 2.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(graphql): cover ClamavQuery/ClamavMutation resolvers (SUPPORT-646 Group 3)\n\nBoth classes had zero unit tests before this change (only the isValidHost\ndelegate was tested, via the existing ClamavMutationExtensionTest). Uses\nMockito.mockStatic(BundleUtils) — already supported by mockito-core 5.14.2''s\ndefault inline mock maker, no new pom dependency.\n\nClamavQueryTest (F13, F14, F15, F19, F20, U8, D3 — one scaffold per Stage 3''s\nown recommendation to avoid duplicating the BundleUtils mock across classes):\n- settings(): config-present and config-absent (-> ClamavConstants defaults).\n- ping(): true/false delegation and service-absent -> false.\n- scanTest(): PASSED/FAILED round-trip including signature; null/empty content\n  and oversize base64 both -> ERROR without ever calling BundleUtils.getOsgiService\n  (verifyNoInteractions pins the short-circuit); malformed base64 -> ERROR after\n  the service lookup but before scan(); service-absent -> CONNECTION_FAILED,\n  proven distinct from all the ERROR cases; an unchecked RuntimeException from\n  scan() -> ERROR (not CONNECTION_FAILED) without propagating.\n\nClamavMutationTest (F16, F18 — new class; ClamavMutationExtensionTest is left\nuntouched per Stage 3''s recommendation, it owns the isValidHost delegate only):\n- saveSettings(): happy path writes every field via a captured Dictionary;\n  partial update (nulls) preserves the prior, non-default values; a rejected\n  host never touches ConfigurationAdmin at all; ConfigurationAdmin.getConfiguration\n  throwing IOException, and the service being absent, both return false without\n  propagating.\n- Port (0, 65536) and timeout (0, MAX_TIMEOUT_MS+1, -5) rejection on\n  saveSettings() itself, each verified to never touch ConfigurationAdmin —\n  distinct from the already-covered host whitelist and from ClamavConfig''s\n  separate OSGi-.cfg-path port/timeout tests.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 3.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add raw-binary/PUT scan and schema-namespace e2e specs (SUPPORT-646 Group 4a)\n\n- 03-clamavFilter-RawBinaryUpload.cy.ts (U1 Cypress half + D2): proves the\n  raw-binary/PUT scanning path (isRawBinaryUpload, SEC-141) actually\n  intercepts a real, non-multipart PUT end to end against a live daemon.\n  Targets the RESTful JCR API''s property-write endpoint against the\n  always-present /users/root node (no site/content provisioning needed\n  beyond what assets/provisioning.yml already installs): a clean raw PUT\n  must not be blocked by ClamavFilter, an EICAR-content PUT (sent as a raw,\n  unescaped body so the exact signature bytes reach the daemon) must be\n  rejected with 403 before ever reaching the JCR-REST handler.\n\n  FLAGGED FOR STAGE 6: the RESTful JCR API is deprecated and closed by\n  default behind the security-filter''s jcrestapi grant, which this module''s\n  provisioning.yml does not configure; whether the Docker test image''s\n  default profile already grants this to a privileged session is\n  unconfirmed without a live run (could not be verified in this stage per\n  the pipeline''s own instructions). The preflight GET is written to fail\n  distinctly from the scan-blocking assertions if this is the gap. The\n  exact HAL response shape is taken from documentation, not a live\n  response, and may need small adjustment.\n\n- 04-clamavFilter-SchemaNamespace.cy.ts (D1): asserts the correct nested\n  clamav{...} shape succeeds and the documented-but-wrong flat\n  clamavSettings/clamavPing field names are rejected by schema validation\n  — turning Stage 2''s manual schema-shape finding into an automated\n  regression canary. Adds two small new GraphQL fixture files for the\n  flat (invalid) queries, following the existing require(''graphql-tag/loader!...'')\n  fixture convention.\n\nBoth specs lint clean (yarn lint / eslint -c .eslintrc.json --ext .ts).\nNot run against the dockerized stack in this stage per the pipeline''s\nStage 5/Stage 6 split.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(js): add first ClamavFilter.jsx test file (SUPPORT-646 Group 4b)\n\nAdds ClamavFilter.test.jsx — the first test file for the ClamavFilterAdmin\ncomponent itself (previously only its child presentational components had\ncoverage). Mocks @apollo/client''s useQuery/useMutation/useLazyQuery hooks\ndirectly (keeping the real gql tag via jest.requireActual) and react-i18next/\n@jahia/moonstone the same way the existing component tests do.\n\n- U5: the 10 MB client-side size gate in handleScan() rejects an oversized\n  synthetic File with a SIZE_ERROR result BEFORE the SCAN_TEST lazy query is\n  ever invoked (the actual untested gap — ScanSection.test.jsx only rendered\n  the SIZE_ERROR prop directly, never exercised the gating logic that\n  produces it). A companion test proves a within-limit file DOES invoke\n  SCAN_TEST, so the gate is proven in both directions.\n- U6 residual: handleFieldBlur''s field-name -> coercion-function mapping —\n  port blurs through clampPort (clamps to 65535), connectionTimeout and\n  readTimeout each blur through coerceTimeout with their OWN min/default pair\n  (100 vs 1000), proving the fields aren''t cross-wired to the wrong coercion\n  call; host has no coercion mapped and is a no-op.\n\nAll 6 new tests pass; full yarn test suite: 5 suites / 36 tests passing.\nyarn lint clean.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* style(cypress): restore eslint-compliant formatting on the new e2e specs\n\nAn automated formatting pass reformatted these two new files to a semi:false/\nspaced-braces style (matching tests/.prettierrc.js) that conflicts with this\nproject''s actual lint gate (yarn lint / eslint -c .eslintrc.json), which\nrequires semicolons and no object-curly-spacing. Re-ran eslint --fix so both\nfiles pass yarn lint again (0 errors); no logical/behavioral change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(tests): open security-filter profile in provisioning so JCR-REST spec runs\n\nStage 6 (SUPPORT-646) wrongly concluded the raw-binary/PUT Cypress spec''s\npreflight 404s were a jcrestapi 3.3.0 platform defect. The real cause: the\nsecurity-filter bundle''s security.profile defaults to ''default'' (closed to\nnon-privileged/external API calls), which blocks the RESTful JCR-REST calls\nthis spec makes and surfaces as confusing 404s/500s instead of a clean 403.\n\nAdd a config:property-set karafCommand to tests/assets/provisioning.yml that\nsets security.profile=open early in provisioning, before Cypress runs (test\ncontainers only, never acceptable for production). Update the spec''s header\ncomment to reflect the correction instead of the stale \"flagged for Stage 6\"\nuncertainty.\n\nVerified live: GET /modules/api/jcr/v1/default/en/paths/users/root now\nreturns 200 (was 404), and 03-clamavFilter-RawBinaryUpload.cy.ts passes both\ntests. Full dockerized Cypress suite: 21/21 passing (was 19/21).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"59ea0f6fbd2224a9ff856986830f7542edc253bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/59ea0f6fbd2224a9ff856986830f7542edc253bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/8302884033d372961a231f3d30527bac6264a94b","verification":{"payload":"tree 59ea0f6fbd2224a9ff856986830f7542edc253bf\nparent e29770ca77a4bd15b09f076d1e7e5808cd2a07b6\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100481 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100481 +0200\n\ntest: add JUnit/Jest/Cypress coverage for fail-closed core, GraphQL resolvers, and admin UI (SUPPORT-646) (#22)\n\n* test(filter,config): cover isRawBinaryUpload and ClamavConfig gaps (SUPPORT-646 Group 1)\n\n- ClamavFilterTest: add the isRawBinaryUpload() 5-row table test (U1 JUnit half) —\n  previously untested despite being the SEC-141 raw-binary/PUT routing predicate.\n- ClamavConfigTest: fix the F9 downgrade by asserting a second updated() call on\n  the same live instance replaces the first (live-reload semantics), add the\n  previously zero-coverage connection_timeout/read_timeout out-of-range rejection\n  branch with atomicity re-checks, and add a partial-update case proving omitted\n  keys retain their prior (non-default) values rather than resetting to defaults.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 1.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(filter): cover ClamavFilter.doFilter fail-closed core (SUPPORT-646 Group 2)\n\nAdds ClamavFilterDoFilterTest, a new shared harness (real multipart bytes parsed\nby a real CommonsMultipartResolver, plain octet-stream/PUT request builders, a\nstreaming-only zero-filled InputStream for the 100 MiB streaming-cap case) plus\n26 tests covering doFilter() end to end, which had zero direct test coverage\nbefore this change despite being the security-critical fail-closed core:\n\n- F1/F3: happy-path forwarding of the WRAPPED request to the chain, with\n  byte-identity proof between what was scanned and the original file content.\n- F2: an attacker-controlled parameter/header has zero effect on whether\n  scanning occurs.\n- F4: both oversize entry paths (declared Content-Length pre-check and the\n  streaming RequestTooLargeException catch) return 413.\n- F5: infected uploads return 403 and the log line is pinned to exactly\n  \"Uploaded file is a malware\" (and asserted to NOT contain the signature,\n  documenting today''s actual, doc-divergent behavior per Stage 2).\n- F6: all four fail-closed scenarios (service never bound, ping()==false,\n  scan()->Status.ERROR), for both the multipart and octet-stream entry paths,\n  with an explicit assertion that scan() is never invoked once ping() has\n  failed (pins the `service == null || !service.ping()` short-circuit order).\n- F7: a genuine MalformedStreamException from a truncated multipart body, and\n  a stream IOException, both resolve to 500.\n- D4: a 12-row parameterized umbrella asserting chain.doFilter() is NEVER\n  invoked across every non-clean outcome enumerated above plus both oversize\n  paths — the single highest-value regression guard in this set, since it\n  generalizes beyond any individually enumerated scenario.\n\nAdds ch.qos.logback:logback-classic as a test-only dependency: the module has\nno SLF4J provider on the unit-test classpath otherwise (it relies on the OSGi\ncontainer''s own logging backend at runtime), so a real Logger implementation is\nneeded to attach a ListAppender for the F5/F7 log-content assertions.\n\nAll 26 new tests pass against the current, unmodified ClamavFilter — the\nfail-closed guarantee held up under from-scratch, adversarial test-writing\nscrutiny; no gap was found in the security-critical core itself.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 2.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(graphql): cover ClamavQuery/ClamavMutation resolvers (SUPPORT-646 Group 3)\n\nBoth classes had zero unit tests before this change (only the isValidHost\ndelegate was tested, via the existing ClamavMutationExtensionTest). Uses\nMockito.mockStatic(BundleUtils) — already supported by mockito-core 5.14.2''s\ndefault inline mock maker, no new pom dependency.\n\nClamavQueryTest (F13, F14, F15, F19, F20, U8, D3 — one scaffold per Stage 3''s\nown recommendation to avoid duplicating the BundleUtils mock across classes):\n- settings(): config-present and config-absent (-> ClamavConstants defaults).\n- ping(): true/false delegation and service-absent -> false.\n- scanTest(): PASSED/FAILED round-trip including signature; null/empty content\n  and oversize base64 both -> ERROR without ever calling BundleUtils.getOsgiService\n  (verifyNoInteractions pins the short-circuit); malformed base64 -> ERROR after\n  the service lookup but before scan(); service-absent -> CONNECTION_FAILED,\n  proven distinct from all the ERROR cases; an unchecked RuntimeException from\n  scan() -> ERROR (not CONNECTION_FAILED) without propagating.\n\nClamavMutationTest (F16, F18 — new class; ClamavMutationExtensionTest is left\nuntouched per Stage 3''s recommendation, it owns the isValidHost delegate only):\n- saveSettings(): happy path writes every field via a captured Dictionary;\n  partial update (nulls) preserves the prior, non-default values; a rejected\n  host never touches ConfigurationAdmin at all; ConfigurationAdmin.getConfiguration\n  throwing IOException, and the service being absent, both return false without\n  propagating.\n- Port (0, 65536) and timeout (0, MAX_TIMEOUT_MS+1, -5) rejection on\n  saveSettings() itself, each verified to never touch ConfigurationAdmin —\n  distinct from the already-covered host whitelist and from ClamavConfig''s\n  separate OSGi-.cfg-path port/timeout tests.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 3.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(cypress): add raw-binary/PUT scan and schema-namespace e2e specs (SUPPORT-646 Group 4a)\n\n- 03-clamavFilter-RawBinaryUpload.cy.ts (U1 Cypress half + D2): proves the\n  raw-binary/PUT scanning path (isRawBinaryUpload, SEC-141) actually\n  intercepts a real, non-multipart PUT end to end against a live daemon.\n  Targets the RESTful JCR API''s property-write endpoint against the\n  always-present /users/root node (no site/content provisioning needed\n  beyond what assets/provisioning.yml already installs): a clean raw PUT\n  must not be blocked by ClamavFilter, an EICAR-content PUT (sent as a raw,\n  unescaped body so the exact signature bytes reach the daemon) must be\n  rejected with 403 before ever reaching the JCR-REST handler.\n\n  FLAGGED FOR STAGE 6: the RESTful JCR API is deprecated and closed by\n  default behind the security-filter''s jcrestapi grant, which this module''s\n  provisioning.yml does not configure; whether the Docker test image''s\n  default profile already grants this to a privileged session is\n  unconfirmed without a live run (could not be verified in this stage per\n  the pipeline''s own instructions). The preflight GET is written to fail\n  distinctly from the scan-blocking assertions if this is the gap. The\n  exact HAL response shape is taken from documentation, not a live\n  response, and may need small adjustment.\n\n- 04-clamavFilter-SchemaNamespace.cy.ts (D1): asserts the correct nested\n  clamav{...} shape succeeds and the documented-but-wrong flat\n  clamavSettings/clamavPing field names are rejected by schema validation\n  — turning Stage 2''s manual schema-shape finding into an automated\n  regression canary. Adds two small new GraphQL fixture files for the\n  flat (invalid) queries, following the existing require(''graphql-tag/loader!...'')\n  fixture convention.\n\nBoth specs lint clean (yarn lint / eslint -c .eslintrc.json --ext .ts).\nNot run against the dockerized stack in this stage per the pipeline''s\nStage 5/Stage 6 split.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test(js): add first ClamavFilter.jsx test file (SUPPORT-646 Group 4b)\n\nAdds ClamavFilter.test.jsx — the first test file for the ClamavFilterAdmin\ncomponent itself (previously only its child presentational components had\ncoverage). Mocks @apollo/client''s useQuery/useMutation/useLazyQuery hooks\ndirectly (keeping the real gql tag via jest.requireActual) and react-i18next/\n@jahia/moonstone the same way the existing component tests do.\n\n- U5: the 10 MB client-side size gate in handleScan() rejects an oversized\n  synthetic File with a SIZE_ERROR result BEFORE the SCAN_TEST lazy query is\n  ever invoked (the actual untested gap — ScanSection.test.jsx only rendered\n  the SIZE_ERROR prop directly, never exercised the gating logic that\n  produces it). A companion test proves a within-limit file DOES invoke\n  SCAN_TEST, so the gate is proven in both directions.\n- U6 residual: handleFieldBlur''s field-name -> coercion-function mapping —\n  port blurs through clampPort (clamps to 65535), connectionTimeout and\n  readTimeout each blur through coerceTimeout with their OWN min/default pair\n  (100 vs 1000), proving the fields aren''t cross-wired to the wrong coercion\n  call; host has no coercion mapped and is a no-op.\n\nAll 6 new tests pass; full yarn test suite: 5 suites / 36 tests passing.\nyarn lint clean.\n\nPart of the SUPPORT-646 test-coverage initiative, Stage 5 Group 4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* style(cypress): restore eslint-compliant formatting on the new e2e specs\n\nAn automated formatting pass reformatted these two new files to a semi:false/\nspaced-braces style (matching tests/.prettierrc.js) that conflicts with this\nproject''s actual lint gate (yarn lint / eslint -c .eslintrc.json), which\nrequires semicolons and no object-curly-spacing. Re-ran eslint --fix so both\nfiles pass yarn lint again (0 errors); no logical/behavioral change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix(tests): open security-filter profile in provisioning so JCR-REST spec runs\n\nStage 6 (SUPPORT-646) wrongly concluded the raw-binary/PUT Cypress spec''s\npreflight 404s were a jcrestapi 3.3.0 platform defect. The real cause: the\nsecurity-filter bundle''s security.profile defaults to ''default'' (closed to\nnon-privileged/external API calls), which blocks the RESTful JCR-REST calls\nthis spec makes and surfaces as confusing 404s/500s instead of a clean 403.\n\nAdd a config:property-set karafCommand to tests/assets/provisioning.yml that\nsets security.profile=open early in provisioning, before Cypress runs (test\ncontainers only, never acceptable for production). Update the spec''s header\ncomment to reflect the correction instead of the stale \"flagged for Stage 6\"\nuncertainty.\n\nVerified live: GET /modules/api/jcr/v1/default/en/paths/users/root now\nreturns 200 (was 404), and 03-clamavFilter-RawBinaryUpload.cy.ts passes both\ntests. Full dockerized Cypress suite: 21/21 passing (was 19/21).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzaBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGKgQAKnMzTf4XKVwdJQD56POMzSd\nywAYhX4QPsdP788BbTdoioRk8bhcyflMypO/wrkArDdesLSAA7pw6qSlBuMLmoZS\nSIZBZkO437JmVY8LemNIdesSUCiEk9kVczXgq9Cf3BBfWU/h04Gm66lEucTvJ3sj\nruB95+XWVCb3nBJRsLyzuV/BI4QcVlLIw4/UywVwLh0uUwh/2Oya/0noashvD6ar\nyUF9+opTs9G3SkrvUVaTBEG0qaDWhDikGsYRQuu3MhCsjyrROfHHmECb/ct0GcK1\nKWdlB2aL+OfBaIqv3Y+F6tzWdBVpbS3hTiTFWoKm1ZLvTPL14cPvV2CGVyxd2X3r\nw2r6nJAi1Hb7zIle5vdxy4/dxvf8qOYOs+HyuEUEGrvP5Nq+R7U1YDnWGjbbBCen\np7b09dVPcu62nA0RixDyJShDtoXtUteDUQ+1bUE//R+PuCNzqn2TBBOestbK8C7l\nNKgP1YKr/ca6GMGvNHgu9BafkK91DCgvxNTcNx6S1pm9j9YYNdVjFD9pRg6z2azf\nDc4uJhUl6ZDgE6VL2BvC9Mmel4E4aaQjDg14uqlr48VXbAym/wnBvgTGF8kjKh0X\nSqXm0i+UzRpyoWeUraQtyFBm6pBqErCA3vSZlEPJ6oVsSLAQErxflPqaHBz9eMuD\nLvW0+pr8DuxWAeUlNIsu\n=STNJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:28:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.c