//avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/e1bd893df0bcf0d031be31d4dd2d18675c375e73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T07:57:29Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T07:57:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: scan raw non-multipart binary uploads (SEC-141 scan-coverage gap) (#20)\n\nThe filter only scanned multipart uploads and one Forms octet-stream path, so malware\ndelivered over a non-multipart binary channel (WebDAV / JCR-REST PUT, application/\noctet-stream bodies) entered the repository UNSCANNED. Generalize the scan trigger to\nalso cover any application/octet-stream body and any PUT carrying a body, routed through\nthe same fail-closed scan path (scanOctetStream).\n\nVerified live on 8.2.4.0-SNAPSHOT with a real clamd: a non-multipart PUT of the EICAR\ntest string (application/octet-stream) is now blocked (HTTP 403, ''Uploaded file is a\nmalware'') where it previously passed through unscanned.\n\nNote: request-shape scanning is inherently partial; repository-level (JCR write) scanning\nremains the fully-robust design and is left for a maintainer-led change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"86b1daf7ad2e2515ee64013cd21070b41999c6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/86b1daf7ad2e2515ee64013cd21070b41999c6aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/e1bd893df0bcf0d031be31d4dd2d18675c375e73","verification":{"payload":"tree 86b1daf7ad2e2515ee64013cd21070b41999c6aa\nparent f56a5d8b16db894c17d84388f5b3ca5dc88ecd6f\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1783497449 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783497449 +0200\n\nfix: scan raw non-multipart binary uploads (SEC-141 scan-coverage gap) (#20)\n\nThe filter only scanned multipart uploads and one Forms octet-stream path, so malware\ndelivered over a non-multipart binary channel (WebDAV / JCR-REST PUT, application/\noctet-stream bodies) entered the repository UNSCANNED. Generalize the scan trigger to\nalso cover any application/octet-stream body and any PUT carrying a body, routed through\nthe same fail-closed scan path (scanOctetStream).\n\nVerified live on 8.2.4.0-SNAPSHOT with a real clamd: a non-multipart PUT of the EICAR\ntest string (application/octet-stream) is now blocked (HTTP 403, ''Uploaded file is a\nmalware'') where it previously passed through unscanned.\n\nNote: request-shape scanning is inherently partial; repository-level (JCR write) scanning\nremains the fully-robust design and is left for a maintainer-led change.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTgLpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsVsQADVuGOabVx91NlVZ1CdHq7e4\nQGbh+FtwxiBvQX0eNByw1kgJWihTRxrWzmU2WmjD4KrD7MvOtBlkmmw4k2B4siBH\n8c3xTBSSVHpfSB0VfzVu++nrJ7/Bdgotr1fUEwAASXabyWYRpt7REERwFk+gc0Ak\nyD+UJohuhBj8k53gDLHML81dbmceAyQPo8DyGO4Wcllq9rAeIJk8U9mBSRGgUT/S\ngQRC