url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b"}],"sha":"f56a5d8b16db894c17d84388f5b3ca5dc88ecd6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/f56a5d8b16db894c17d84388f5b3ca5dc88ecd6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T12:43:45Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T12:43:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: harden clamav-filter (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests, Java 17) (#15)\n\n* chore: harden clamav-filter across quality, a11y, security, tests and Java 17 build\n\nBlind multi-level review remediation (architecture, security, code quality,\nergonomy, accessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation).\n\nSecurity / concurrency (Java):\n- Fix multipart AV-bypass: scan every uploaded part via getMultiFileMap()\n  instead of getFileMap(), which collapsed multiple files sharing a field name\n  and left the extras unscanned but replayed downstream.\n- Make the ClamavService reference volatile with a safe unbind; build a\n  per-request CommonsMultipartResolver (the shared instance was not thread-safe).\n- Unify scanMultipart/scanOctetStream into one fail-closed scanStreams().\n- GraphQL: catch invalid base64 specifically (warn, not error), link the ERROR\n  status string to Status.ERROR.name(), declare the DS service explicitly,\n  and use pattern-matching instanceof.\n\nBuild:\n- Target Java 17 (maven.compiler.release=17) and add SonarQube properties so\n  `mvn clean install sonar:sonar` runs without -D flags.\n\nFrontend (accessibility AAA + ergonomy + quality):\n- Decompose the admin screen into ConnectionSettingsForm/PingSection/ScanSection\n  (component complexity 30 -> within limit) with PropTypes.\n- AAA contrast fixes, 44px target sizes, scroll-margin-top, <output> live\n  regions, status-message staleness fix, contextual file-name announcement,\n  and valid-range hints.\n- Numeric inputs no longer snap back to defaults while being retyped.\n- Remove console statements; repair `yarn lint` (strip-ansi resolution pins).\n\nTests:\n- Add jest + React Testing Library (28 tests) for the decomposed components and\n  the form-coercion helpers.\n- Add Java tests for the multipart fix (collectFiles) and the request size cap\n  (MultiReadHttpServletRequest); add Mockito.\n\nDocs: refresh AGENTS.md / README (version, clamavAdmin permission, Java 17).\n\nAll gates green: SonarQube quality gate OK (0 issues), yarn lint clean,\n28 jest + 73 Java tests, Cypress 15/15.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback (stream handling, timeout clamping, ping UX)\n\nCode review of PR #15 + github-code-quality findings:\n\n- ClamavFilter: open each multipart file stream lazily inside its own\n  try-with-resources and scan via a shared classify() helper. Removes the\n  eager up-front stream collection (which leaked already-opened streams if a\n  later getInputStream() failed) and the double-close in the old scanStreams.\n- formHelpers.coerceTimeout: floor to a per-field minimum and cap at the\n  server MAX_TIMEOUT (300000), so a zero/negative/over-range value is corrected\n  client-side instead of triggering a silent server rejection.\n- ClamavFilter UI: handlePing no longer clears saveStatus — testing the\n  connection must not wipe a still-relevant save banner.\n- MultiReadHttpServletRequestTest: readAll() now owns and closes its stream\n  (try-with-resources) to satisfy the resource-leak check.\n- Add jest tests for the timeout floor/cap behaviour.\n\nRe-verified: SonarQube gate OK (0 issues), yarn lint clean, 30 jest + 73 Java\ntests, build SUCCESS (JDK 17), Cypress 15/15.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee3387f13a49b7632613b0ebbca3266b6a3b7bfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/ee3387f13a49b7632613b0ebbca3266b6a3b7bfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b","verification":{"payload":"tree ee3387f13a49b7632613b0ebbca3266b6a3b7bfe\nparent 737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781873025 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781873025 +0200\n\nchore: harden clamav-filter (security, a11y AAA, quality, tests, Java 17) (#15)\n\n* chore: harden clamav-filter across quality, a11y, security, tests and Java 17 build\n\nBlind multi-level review remediation (architecture, security, code quality,\nergonomy, accessibility AAA, test coverage, documentation).\n\nSecurity / concurrency (Java):\n- Fix multipart AV-bypass: scan every uploaded part via getMultiFileMap()\n  instead of getFileMap(), which collapsed multiple files sharing a field name\n  and left the extras unscanned but replayed downstream.\n- Make the ClamavService reference volatile with a safe unbind; build a\n  per-request CommonsMultipartResolver (the shared instance was not thread-safe).\n- Unify scanMultipart/scanOctetStream into one fail-closed scanStreams().\n- GraphQL: catch invalid base64 specifically (warn, not error), link the ERROR\n  status string to Status.ERROR.name(), declare the DS service explicitly,\n  and use pattern-matching instanceof.\n\nBuild:\n- Target Java 17 (maven.compiler.release=17) and add SonarQube properties so\n  `mvn clean install sonar:sonar` runs without -D flags.\n\nFrontend (accessibility AAA + ergonomy + quality):\n- Decompose the admin screen into ConnectionSettingsForm/PingSection/ScanSection\n  (component complexity 30 -> within limit) with PropTypes.\n- AAA contrast fixes, 44px target sizes, scroll-margin-top, <output> live\n  regions, status-message staleness fix, contextual file-name announcement,\n  and valid-range hints.\n- Numeric inputs no longer snap back to defaults while being retyped.\n- Remove console statements; repair `yarn lint` (strip-ansi resolution pins).\n\nTests:\n- Add jest + React Testing Library (28 tests) for the decomposed components and\n  the form-coercion helpers.\n- Add Java tests for the multipart fix (collectFiles) and the request size cap\n  (MultiReadHttpServletRequest); add Mockito.\n\nDocs: refresh AGENTS.md / README (version, clamavAdmin permission, Java 17).\n\nAll gates green: SonarQube quality gate OK (0 issues), yarn lint clean,\n28 jest + 73 Java tests, Cypress 15/15.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review feedback (stream handling, timeout clamping, ping UX)\n\nCode review of PR #15 + github-code-quality findings:\n\n- ClamavFilter: open each multipart file stream lazily inside its own\n  try-with-resources and scan via a shared classify() helper. Removes the\n  eager up-front stream collection (which leaked already-opened streams if a\n  later getInputStream() failed) and the double-close in the old scanStreams.\n- formHelpers.coerceTimeout: floor to a per-field minimum and cap at the\n  server MAX_TIMEOUT (300000), so a zero/negative/over-range value is corrected\n  client-side instead of triggering a silent server rejection.\n- ClamavFilter UI: handlePing no longer clears saveStatus — testing the\n  connection must not wipe a still-relevant save banner.\n- MultiReadHttpServletRequestTest: readAll() now owns and closes its stream\n  (try-with-resources) to satisfy the resource-leak check.\n- Add jest tests for the timeout floor/cap behaviour.\n\nRe-verified: SonarQube gate OK (0 issues), yarn lint clean, 30 jest + 73 Java\ntests, build SUCCESS (JDK 17), Cypress 15/15.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNTmBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACx4QAKuFHc4QiUPUZMh6RXqihaf/\nv8hsBwPrT+cOJ71iKH37hSPi8Wqnrzu8ZRrpvcJJHsFjk/I0TIpsqmUhO093OET5\nuf6aaIpu8zRpdxBnEf++FM9Zz6GlQpbefZD6eriGUSKnYqfi7njfiManueVH/BYb\nszTHJIAG+egO7FxrgtuHHk3iA2JYmlU/MqlArvUEkDW8rzK8kcI9SuonXAdRzMbd\nn6iQywDLYDyRqa6zmm/RTDAEmHWk+I7Au3MulLYyxyxSpg+j+m+w9wauvt9EjVjx\n8vmHtJghrIc16o+4/moBzORSQ9cvI9eROaFYWqDldK3cCZFww4p6mBEsESk0Ukuo\nsZmQUlmitD1kti7KPEThT+66djO+0PPFq5hT4dBGRp+PML4FI1dLibwL+SB0ArcS\n4lLnQL4kL13kK4HSnuMlCoRt3WBRJY9BkANtGwGKj8hExkVr3D2Hvk49KY2rBZg/\nli+vJVnW6qwTL3YBMIAmX//Cu1pGzg5uTLzn26MlKXULk4EM4ytsJmX9IlK/4ye5\nFEPiKI6e9OZ25qOiqIOfKCc+hu18wS6GakjBBU7P36F1yLM2US6EYJfm0gHe9X67\n4WVnUKPaezQ09OdE6YwPt/ecfUnPbW8ocP5MvnzrFwz9FMgTudrz3Zkxi3r6ScZq\n3GEYpLUmZ/xCnsHdi/d3\n=f1sa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T12:43:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDBjM2YxZjI1YzhiOTZhNTM5NDI1MjliYjM4NGJmNzk3YWIyNjlkMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839","sha":"737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839"}],"sha":"0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/0c3f1f25c8b96a53942529bb384bf797ab269d1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:07:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#14)\n\nAdd regression coverage for the module-specific `clamavAdmin` permission and\nship an assignable admin role so the gate can be granted without full server\nadministrator rights.\n\n- tests/cypress/e2e/02-clamavFilter-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests proving\n  fine-grained enforcement with a user granted ONLY the module role (never\n  `admin`):\n  * GraphQL: denies the gated read-only `clamavSettings` query for a user\n    without the permission, and allows it for the granted user.\n  * Admin UI: hides the /jahia/administration/clamavFilter panel from a user\n    without the permission, and shows it for the granted user.\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new assignable `clamav-filter-administrator`\n  server role granting `administrationAccess clamavAdmin` (admin UI + API).\n- ClamavFilter.scanMultipart: scan via Spring''s Commons-parsed MultipartFile\n  map (getFileMap()) instead of the Servlet 3.0 getParts() API. getParts()\n  threw IllegalStateException on endpoints whose servlet has no multipart\n  config (e.g. /modules/api/provisioning), 500-ing those requests; the\n  Commons-parsed map scans the same files without that dependency. This\n  unblocks the standard @jahia/cypress test-user provisioning used by the\n  new spec. All existing multipart scan tests (clean/EICAR) still pass.\n- pom.xml: bump module version to 1.0.4-SNAPSHOT.\n\nValidated: ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh -> 15/15 specs pass\n(01-clamavFilter 11/11, 02-clamavFilter-Permissions 4/4), license healthy.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"f64e9be6f11b0d11de99fa9d82fcfb4035e62e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/f64e9be6f11b0d11de99fa9d82fcfb4035e62e0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839","verification":{"payload":"tree f64e9be6f11b0d11de99fa9d82fcfb4035e62e0a\nparent 19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118427 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118427 +0200\n\ntest: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#14)\n\nAdd regression coverage for the module-specific `clamavAdmin` permission and\nship an assignable admin role so the gate can be granted without full server\nadministrator rights.\n\n- tests/cypress/e2e/02-clamavFilter-Permissions.cy.ts: 4 tests proving\n  fine-grained enforcement with a user granted ONLY the module role (never\n  `admin`):\n  * GraphQL: denies the gated read-only `clamavSettings` query for a user\n    without the permission, and allows it for the granted user.\n  * Admin UI: hides the /jahia/administration/clamavFilter panel from a user\n    without the permission, and shows it for the granted user.\n- src/main/import/roles.xml: new assignable `clamav-filter-administrator`\n  server role granting `administrationAccess clamavAdmin` (admin UI + API).\n- ClamavFilter.scanMultipart: scan via Spring''s Commons-parsed MultipartFile\n  map (getFileMap()) instead of the Servlet 3.0 getParts() API. getParts()\n  threw IllegalStateException on endpoints whose servlet has no multipart\n  config (e.g. /modules/api/provisioning), 500-ing those requests; the\n  Commons-parsed map scans the same files without that dependency. This\n  unblocks the standard @jahia/cypress test-user provisioning used by the\n  new spec. All existing multipart scan tests (clean/EICAR) still pass.\n- pom.xml: bump module version to 1.0.4-SNAPSHOT.\n\nValidated: ./ci.build.sh && ./ci.startup.sh -> 15/15 specs pass\n(01-clamavFilter 11/11, 02-clamavFilter-Permissions 4/4), license healthy.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbXbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt2MQAI05B/Z05wmR592lUArrzPJe\nAaIreNsUotUklsKTJ5TRsrr3A4qE2V4fVh6hV3GS9wCmfHTqZTfgPwmECzvMYw/U\n4QS7QmKDRr24rLre8W2R43e+zOE/7G5/1cLlUFD5ZZxXTGNLntF7EsHHzQxxB8eM\nvXmzpDD86PrHCib0zveexBOH2UZkAfq8vGfOpeKb22z7wLO1D5M4pS6EcYSM0390\nGu1KbOCOo2A5FXap+ZO5KuyLqN1B3XzcvM2kW4oSA+htxeM5VtHMTOYEeTdqI3Ee\nB8W5TIly/0tI0CgXilh8DuOkRoyMABnzM0yl0l57q1IrNGKTfnGdverSSmxSjLjg\nrEAaXowYjpX8M8BrgIFdjh4MIfmEMvSMv4ECRpiiCXtx7mXs64qfCT3Lhsf4hEVY\nwtP7ZFffGTJFGEdLm4cQ4eA0ThO84Ka0f8GAhkWQn0JyDrpuzwwy9Wi9WjWaM3Km\ncENR7hdSuzLV1mGGR7z0es6NM/FberJjUUnJzlkT69ocxHwDgPIo7W9LRcX9PrPM\nFgpekl2A0eLZ/SZoXoV44pVNCKXyK7cak/bmypnYsRm6sFCk1EhAayMKCH5s7O+W\nDl1LYLX2At1dY88wbXWAhngfQ4TtF5OLSwmnFr+4kDou55yFSxs8NVSzD1fPhLn2\nP7W0tnXG86YizxyXQozU\n=e9X3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:07:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839","node_id":"C_kwDOMMR5ENoAKDczN2Q3MzRlYzVkZWVmZTIwZWQzNjE4MGFhNWQ4N2FmOGQxN2M4Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/clamav-filter/commit/19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf","sha":"19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf"}],"sha":"737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/737d734ec5deefe20ed36180aa5d87af8d17c839"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/commits/19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T09:41:43Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T09:41:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add module-specific clamavAdmin permission for fine-grained RBAC (#13)\n\n* feat: add module-specific clamavAdmin permission for fine-grained RBAC\n\nDefine clamavAdmin as a JCR child permission of admin in\nsrc/main/import/permissions.xml so that non-admin users can be granted\nonly the ClamAV management permission. Update all four\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission annotations from \"admin\" to \"clamavAdmin\".\nFull admins retain access through JCR privilege inheritance.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"e80af46ec184cf0431ac6c9f098dc498cd125a03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/trees/e80af46ec184cf0431ac6c9f098dc498cd125a03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/clamav-filter/git/commits/19fe0c0b88b3f2d2eb42ffb84b24288175d861bf","verification":{"payload":"tree e80af46ec184cf0431ac6c9f098dc498cd125a03\nparent 5878998371479a971efa12dc398f34a0f5967a26\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781084503 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781084503 +0200\n\nfeat: add module-specific clamavAdmin permission for fine-grained RBAC (#13)\n\n* feat: add module-specific clamavAdmin permission for fine-grained RBAC\n\nDefine clamavAdmin as a JCR child permission of admin in\nsrc/main/import/permissions.xml so that non-admin users can be granted\nonly the ClamAV management permission. Update all four\n@GraphQLRequiresPermission annotations from \"admin\" to \"clamavAdmin\".\nFull admins retain access through JCR privilege inheritance.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: update requiredPermission to module-specific permission in frontend registration\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKTFXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHA0QAETJMeceGYqFVB1cXbX4xuaN\nLm3Ag3+CdcNxvoy9n8zuP9V2XGqJ7ip8dR7nTnsLiFGb6RwqQud/3SR7KxLnLGMj\ntfTaPUomKt3NJzVyRghygM6SiP1LhB1PoS0fZZ3CEXQ+oR9PEyxrHfgBrQdOmTyj\nnGJ5OruYIaeBltIj1dY0O8W8T4BTNF4Ay9fWUjFRbYNuupvfVknFlwszhnciESQ3\n5T9a34pr6eUzWtjwx3fDD0rluA9huXAAIGT37z0nYiKuUDirlB+UkEkFNzW04T72\nyUYsedUPTJ9nJcoHNM6u0rpD+HEIHpoOPUV5iortsg1wEgG0JHsMh+sYf7JhD4UR\n2E80SOuUpyiTqRlAvG0ys+vnQ7PYd5Msguyj2rFBORZ2cGGJZTFTdI/ELTA8266B\nJsRv94J4NuF1kybHrPiOEbtZ0hbwrTz9URmo+jtDE9ua0sDySfTxZFjdxxHhOqTZ\nm5GJtbU5f7mWRe3NisIThx5F0FYyTUw0b+DAIXfBXNVv01Xsqhm3Ra9lArPKM/pW\nQnB4PrB2tWAPxICX25IKBPc+M6hcs4Vz0+1xehxhZzRkiZfvQOyKkqy0guj0dsJc\nY8SIe3JqjgDeoKd8uZNhgNM3mgHXiBLrr1TM3JyVfEOBZzjuxFzCjioB/5zX33nD\ndhMVNvCR0HmU5uE6EmMv\n=TuXE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-10T09:41:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User