s://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/julianocosta89","id":15364991,"login":"julianocosta89","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzY0OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianocosta89","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/plugins/commits/40d09762a10c05480bb8c7acead8b8b941b4b46b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:34:13Z","email":"julianocosta89@outlook.com","name":"Juliano Costa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:34:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[FEATURE] Prometheus: add Exemplars support (#799)\n\n* feat(prometheus): add exemplars spec section and queryExemplars client method\n\nAdd an optional `exemplars: { enable: boolean }` section to the\nPrometheusDatasource spec, exposed in the datasource editor as a\ntoggle and validated by the CUE schema.\n\nAdd a `queryExemplars` method to the Prometheus client hitting\nGET /api/v1/query_exemplars with the same query parameters and\nauthentication handling as the other API calls. The endpoint is also\nadded to the default proxy allowedEndpoints list.\n\nRelated to perses/perses#3445\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* feat(prometheus): fetch exemplars in PrometheusTimeSeriesQuery\n\nWhen the selected datasource has exemplars enabled in its spec and the\nquery runs in range mode, fire a query_exemplars request alongside the\nrange query (same PromQL and time range, in parallel) and attach the\nconverted exemplar data to the returned TimeSeriesData.\n\nExemplar timestamps are converted from seconds to ms and values are\nparsed as numbers. A failing exemplar request never breaks the panel:\nthe error is logged and the query result is returned without exemplars.\n\nRelated to perses/perses#3445\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Move exemplars section into General Settings in PrometheusDatasourceEditor\n\nAddress maintainer feedback from PR #799: the Exemplars heading and\ntoggle now render before HTTPSettingsEditor as part of the General\nSettings section.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* [DOC] Document the exemplars support in the Prometheus plugin\n\nAdd a functional documentation section about the new exemplars support:\nopt-in at the datasource level, fetched in parallel of range queries via\n/api/v1/query_exemplars and rendered as pin-able diamond markers on the\nTime Series Chart.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Address review feedback: handle exemplar failures eagerly and mirror exemplars in the Go SDK\n\n- Attach the rejection handler when the exemplar promise is created so a\n  fast-failing /api/v1/query_exemplars request cannot surface as an\n  unhandled rejection while the range query is still running\n- Ignore exemplar responses that resolve with an error status\n- Add the exemplars field to the PrometheusDatasource Go SDK PluginSpec\n  along with the EnableExemplars() builder option, test and docs\n- Document exemplars in docs/prometheus/model.md and the Go SDK doc\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* [DOC] Describe the exemplar metadata dialog interaction\n\nClicking an exemplar marker opens the ExemplarMetadataDialog with the\nseries labels, exemplar labels, value and timestamp; it does not pin\nthe chart tooltip. Align the docs with the actual TimeSeriesChart\nbehavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Fix CI: repair exemplars doc link and format get-time-series-data.ts\n\n- The exemplars concept link pointed to https://prometheus.io/docs/concepts/exemplars/\n  which returns 404. Point it to the Prometheus exemplars API docs instead.\n- Fix the exemplar-storage feature flag anchor (#exemplar-storage -> #exemplars-storage).\n- Apply oxfmt formatting to get-time-series-data.ts.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>","tree":{"sha":"301b7b55897c2038e9a365110b9c17563268cb7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/plugins/git/trees/301b7b55897c2038e9a365110b9c17563268cb7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/perses/plugins/git/commits/40d09762a10c05480bb8c7acead8b8b941b4b46b","verification":{"payload":"tree 301b7b55897c2038e9a365110b9c17563268cb7f\nparent 84dc97ecb9480c10a566842e996cc3d4f6ad8392\nauthor Juliano Costa <julianocosta89@outlook.com> 1789655653 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789655653 +0000\n\n[FEATURE] Prometheus: add Exemplars support (#799)\n\n* feat(prometheus): add exemplars spec section and queryExemplars client method\n\nAdd an optional `exemplars: { enable: boolean }` section to the\nPrometheusDatasource spec, exposed in the datasource editor as a\ntoggle and validated by the CUE schema.\n\nAdd a `queryExemplars` method to the Prometheus client hitting\nGET /api/v1/query_exemplars with the same query parameters and\nauthentication handling as the other API calls. The endpoint is also\nadded to the default proxy allowedEndpoints list.\n\nRelated to perses/perses#3445\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* feat(prometheus): fetch exemplars in PrometheusTimeSeriesQuery\n\nWhen the selected datasource has exemplars enabled in its spec and the\nquery runs in range mode, fire a query_exemplars request alongside the\nrange query (same PromQL and time range, in parallel) and attach the\nconverted exemplar data to the returned TimeSeriesData.\n\nExemplar timestamps are converted from seconds to ms and values are\nparsed as numbers. A failing exemplar request never breaks the panel:\nthe error is logged and the query result is returned without exemplars.\n\nRelated to perses/perses#3445\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Move exemplars section into General Settings in PrometheusDatasourceEditor\n\nAddress maintainer feedback from PR #799: the Exemplars heading and\ntoggle now render before HTTPSettingsEditor as part of the General\nSettings section.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* [DOC] Document the exemplars support in the Prometheus plugin\n\nAdd a functional documentation section about the new exemplars support:\nopt-in at the datasource level, fetched in parallel of range queries via\n/api/v1/query_exemplars and rendered as pin-able diamond markers on the\nTime Series Chart.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Address review feedback: handle exemplar failures eagerly and mirror exemplars in the Go SDK\n\n- Attach the rejection handler when the exemplar promise is created so a\n  fast-failing /api/v1/query_exemplars request cannot surface as an\n  unhandled rejection while the range query is still running\n- Ignore exemplar responses that resolve with an error status\n- Add the exemplars field to the PrometheusDatasource Go SDK PluginSpec\n  along with the EnableExemplars() builder option, test and docs\n- Document exemplars in docs/prometheus/model.md and the Go SDK doc\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* [DOC] Describe the exemplar metadata dialog interaction\n\nClicking an exemplar marker opens the ExemplarMetadataDialog with the\nseries labels, exemplar labels, value and timestamp; it does not pin\nthe chart tooltip. Align the docs with the actual TimeSeriesChart\nbehavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n* Fix CI: repair exemplars doc link and format get-time-series-data.ts\n\n- The exemplars concept link pointed to https://prometheus.io/docs/concepts/exemplars/\n  which returns 404. Point it to the Prometheus exemplars API docs instead.\n- Fix the exemplar-storage feature flag anchor (#exemplar-storage -> #exemplars-storage).\n- Apply oxfmt formatting to get-time-series-data.ts.\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Juliano Costa <juliano.costa@datadoghq.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq/p0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV20QABe2UXbkT9UOzsFe236oApZc\nVmYU7zoXuUgv/xmPxsGkCjjDkWndIYj0+wWJYJqTg1pBHmb5YqE6AnPa37TvXNRw\nSpC+seFwdoSUnD4O9h3LrU5udPMsHQLP2wkKrjvCpZ7us16QYZkMdaOFrFNP3uGo\n3dBlpC7CxXRrpBC3UlrkmB0AuRPltmJOhCmzLZ6HrdJvRUMXT5sYpvK6DhBmXDzz\nkQ/sx867GZkPw9UXY9sIl5cnux+AoDKzltzDKw64YoBZJtL/2vwf8XUrh7y4YjLm\nkZ3nzTeTpDjsl7IEoOnM0wI38hfzsRJUQoq2gBT+/I1uw1VGzrwGwV4j9INmtmbL\nUEdPyAgwTKizX7tKBBD2r+aeVZ/WMjMUE0jfEcVOm1shIpUt9etrNxS/EPr53eVe\nXF1mgMkVo+oerICqwINcIFaMAh2Okohh+sOSEL15kCXZIpYWbbi8Fw5V+ZD6hBr/\nNaisqLjZh8zdYkzGEpoub+tXf/DYx+xHetv2499ATI5Q3ESnxULoedghrh8Y9dk+\n4N6Hf8Q/L/YcF3cq1H5xTAZt2Hlaeqky3Wy4R6DaKoPoCoxLsLdqMHiqQ5/3zPq2\nkZ3bgMGarvuplHPjtfakpmPw2/WYEAh/30Soum4IMTLphQNgx85wJXMKl+yR4muj\nVW5BhoGZkx5PWaM7N5Ur\n=5Myy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T14:34:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gis