sts{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/307c4d7d0520b0c9efcb57f139e29a38eff41af4","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDMwN2M0ZDdkMDUyMGIwYzllZmNiNTdmMTM5ZTI5YTM4ZWZmNDFhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03","sha":"092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03"}],"sha":"307c4d7d0520b0c9efcb57f139e29a38eff41af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/307c4d7d0520b0c9efcb57f139e29a38eff41af4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:05:40Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:05:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: use electrum as default chain source (#2595)\n\n* fix: use electrum as default chain source\n\nElectrum is less resource heavy than esplora and works just as well.\nLDK_ELECTRUM_SERVER now defaults to the Alby electrum server and\nLDK_ESPLORA_SERVER becomes the opt-in override.\n\nThe unused-address check and auto swap xpub lookahead previously\ncalled the esplora REST API regardless of the configured chain\nsource. They now go through a chain.AddressLookup that follows the\nsame selection as LDK: esplora if configured, otherwise electrum\n(via go-electrum''s blockchain.scripthash.get_history). Bitcoind has\nno address index so it also falls back to electrum, with a warning\nlogged at startup.\n\nCloses #2563\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: clarify address lookup server for bitcoind\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove esplora override from raspberry pi installers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: replace go-electrum client to avoid goroutine leak on close\n\nThe pinned go-electrum client leaks its transport listener goroutine\non every Shutdown(): it blocks forever sending the closed-connection\nerror on an unbuffered channel nobody reads. As the address lookup\nopens and closes a client per check, these accumulated for the\nlifetime of the process.\n\nReplace it with a minimal synchronous JSON-RPC client that reads\nresponses on the caller''s goroutine, so closing it leaves nothing\nrunning. Adds a regression test with a mock electrum server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa20503d520b701c4560b3dd45133914bcf18e31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/fa20503d520b701c4560b3dd45133914bcf18e31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03","verification":{"payload":"tree fa20503d520b701c4560b3dd45133914bcf18e31\nparent 0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1790154340 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790154340 +0700\n\nfix: use electrum as default chain source (#2595)\n\n* fix: use electrum as default chain source\n\nElectrum is less resource heavy than esplora and works just as well.\nLDK_ELECTRUM_SERVER now defaults to the Alby electrum server and\nLDK_ESPLORA_SERVER becomes the opt-in override.\n\nThe unused-address check and auto swap xpub lookahead previously\ncalled the esplora REST API regardless of the configured chain\nsource. They now go through a chain.AddressLookup that follows the\nsame selection as LDK: esplora if configured, otherwise electrum\n(via go-electrum''s blockchain.scripthash.get_history). Bitcoind has\nno address index so it also falls back to electrum, with a warning\nlogged at startup.\n\nCloses #2563\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: clarify address lookup server for bitcoind\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove esplora override from raspberry pi installers\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: replace go-electrum client to avoid goroutine leak on close\n\nThe pinned go-electrum client leaks its transport listener goroutine\non every Shutdown(): it blocks forever sending the closed-connection\nerror on an unbuffered channel nobody reads. As the address lookup\nopens and closes a client per check, these accumulated for the\nlifetime of the process.\n\nReplace it with a minimal synchronous JSON-RPC client that reads\nresponses on the caller''s goroutine, so closing it leaves nothing\nrunning. Adds a regression test with a mock electrum server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5ZkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxhwQAC3ln+Lug7axdHMTxSUf0qaS\nzytLAlAVd4ayHN4Is8DCWzPWCu9LzCTK3oDGdbJ0+fBBXIMj6K5mxGLHDiQQlg/r\nx8eN4514SRR1w7xtOhBQXf5BaIHvOkDKtda+tY7rUHHYCQe2Er0nxIMVSFGexKC7\nhta70ok69oHEn9O6BGE5aWnXbNg9LxrUt67qVpKa6oCvQms9HJ/C6ppnOC7/pl2F\nJ+S7lNc7lZ8BT8UQIQroarSAyA5OvhBiCdYG9ucmIGhRIIz7MsQ8rM0/T/W7vAvC\nvSaOQ5Cd5kME3HIDSXkeyghp0dlG0KXCoz3aBbSrG+zlELW+8NR6wQqe3Owta71n\n6UwJ03rE3AUYCctNE80dM8/XLEbG1ASM63vh9G8FSA0OvcltXrYxXDpqROtL6Dnq\nhcv7cM2kLSbltbg8mLMGT0eeiNPzB2rLKp0KrNfEVSbKjCNJRxF4xEVLLfUd05Fr\nY/3dGKu6vTBh9+tbt2V8EcZGqnxEIeyEUH7hMS9dfFsZFnSfyaPDBhohqUzjRh0A\nTCSnaJsWMfoAB/5I2cLQEGG8aBBNxOtvTU0AQTWLVvO/yF83McTTf71+WX1rWpeN\nXiR41JkuBkFgrCzmB+GmjSR1cN8jYaL7nnp9qkyALfxX6/cSLJI5MU8IDIwV5d+s\nMY2YTQvlHZHKBv6fwRiJ\n=DIl1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T09:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDA5MjA3NDYwMzc5NmNiNWEyNTViZTRiYjgxNTNjZGZhMGM0NWZlMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864","sha":"0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864"}],"sha":"092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/092074603796cb5a255be4bb8153cdfa0c45fe03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130258664?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PeteClubSeven","id":130258664,"login":"PeteClubSeven","node_id":"U_kgDOB8OW6A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PeteClubSeven","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:02:45Z","email":"130258664+PeteClubSeven@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:02:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: update bark bindings to v0.24.0 (#2599)\n\nBump gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark-ffi-bindings/golang from v0.15.0 to\nv0.24.0. The API surface we use is unchanged across the jump (movements,\nlightning send/receive states and notifications are all identical), so\nthe bump itself needs no adaptation, but two new APIs are worth adopting:\n\n- Shutdown now calls StopDaemonWait instead of StopDaemon, so the daemon''s\n  background tasks are finished before we free the wallet. The work\n  directory is wiped and replaced on the next start when a backup restore\n  is pending, so nothing should still be writing to the datadir.\n\n- The recoveryreport node command now reads RecoveryStatus. Previously a\n  nil RecoveryReport was reported as \"no recovery scan ran\", but a nil\n  report also means the scan errored, which can leave funds unrecovered.\n  Those two cases are now distinguished, and a failed scan says so and\n  surfaces the error.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc7fdbbe175ec8b8e2099ef1317f0713006aa49d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/fc7fdbbe175ec8b8e2099ef1317f0713006aa49d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/0709bf026cf83e7407ddd224413e5961a370f864","verification":{"payload":"tree fc7fdbbe175ec8b8e2099ef1317f0713006aa49d\nparent 7d6fd083bc055fd4d24361c394d568cf7295df56\nauthor Peter <130258664+PeteClubSeven@users.noreply.github.com> 1790154165 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790154165 +0700\n\nchore: update bark bindings to v0.24.0 (#2599)\n\nBump gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark-ffi-bindings/golang from v0.15.0 to\nv0.24.0. The API surface we use is unchanged across the jump (movements,\nlightning send/receive states and notifications are all identical), so\nthe bump itself needs no adaptation, but two new APIs are worth adopting:\n\n- Shutdown now calls StopDaemonWait instead of StopDaemon, so the daemon''s\n  background tasks are finished before we free the wallet. The work\n  directory is wiped and replaced on the next start when a backup restore\n  is pending, so nothing should still be writing to the datadir.\n\n- The recoveryreport node command now reads RecoveryStatus. Previously a\n  nil RecoveryReport was reported as \"no recovery scan ran\", but a nil\n  report also means the scan errored, which can leave funds unrecovered.\n  Those two cases are now distinguished, and a failed scan says so and\n  surfaces the error.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5W1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOuYQALHlFchWlguwsR/P0jDUB/9m\nK2gl+2GbPTvxTFrS5PFPerRjPh6aDnCmZpPLrDpD1LQ1C/Z5WUB0vRCFBUpBmBX8\nrRKb80DlNN5eUWcxyaVtVK7ey3Qkb/fBUKWhH9IXV+++f6CFejU+OrGCLkRPXVFO\nYHy7q4QCI7PqvogcIhIN8n8bSOUXh7+U18bQrkYvRtoFTMzeAWZLOuscUcQ0DoJ+\nkubez+2/iaYswdEbHhKP+3Rsl70MOm75zyBdkawFEDaCvU4kXI6PZTOI075HkTGG\nP0+U81voy+o9JJT02RhpXv9+pIoGCxn0ZTZTIMfGAUpijXDGRun4Sn322BnTElIl\nguCVF+TQj5BWhBzK4syELQXqdkomXkxE4GikVgP7KzWYrnyOBE34SLLAdNir+Pua\nqFoDuGH0Ds8uFUotqZVlvA076RtnwbzcgKX4tRkUqA9dSpqUGYOGiQPAAdQG3NX5\niJnOdvsyfhxozXWH+4JJvnlGkoC2X7PXs5YesXa/hzjTDWscUCsTLAYfKF5civfN\n+6a/bdgYiISCDrbLaLej3JRPcAOE+WUzEVrxEZfgEpSJpwJIPc/Be8HOVptRqGMF\n0I3UDdz2H0cB9Gy7PhQBuxV62GbFdkCtkuODZGxgj9OscZcEVFXGJMg55CWdm1eq\nM3TzI1S1OsU10TV8DJCn\n=TDh4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T09:02:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_