d the top-level files of the LDK storage\ndirectory (ldk/storage), so the static channel backup snapshots written\nto the sibling ldk/static_channel_backups directory were never included\nand were lost after migrating to another device.\n\nLNClient.GetStorageDir now returns the backend''s real working directory\n(as Bark already did) and CreateBackup archives that whole tree\nrecursively, still excluding log files. The directory is verified to be\ninside the hub workdir since archive entries are stored relative to it.\n\nFixes #2573\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: fail node migration on non-regular files in storage dir\n\nOnly regular files are expected in the LNClient storage directory:\nsymlinks could point outside the workdir and special files cannot be\ncopied. Fail the backup instead of silently omitting them so the user\nnotices that the migration file would be incomplete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b797fc39b9cd7f15f82631f7f60f61f5c23e4324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/b797fc39b9cd7f15f82631f7f60f61f5c23e4324"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/5c32e566cbf7a0228e348700f658b7dac537d28f","verification":{"payload":"tree b797fc39b9cd7f15f82631f7f60f61f5c23e4324\nparent 06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1788335926 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788335926 +0700\n\nfix: include static channel backups in node migration file (#2574)\n\n* fix: include static channel backups in node migration file\n\nThe migration file only archived the top-level files of the LDK storage\ndirectory (ldk/storage), so the static channel backup snapshots written\nto the sibling ldk/static_channel_backups directory were never included\nand were lost after migrating to another device.\n\nLNClient.GetStorageDir now returns the backend''s real working directory\n(as Bark already did) and CreateBackup archives that whole tree\nrecursively, still excluding log files. The directory is verified to be\ninside the hub workdir since archive entries are stored relative to it.\n\nFixes #2573\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: fail node migration on non-regular files in storage dir\n\nOnly regular files are expected in the LNClient storage directory:\nsymlinks could point outside the workdir and special files cannot be\ncopied. Fail the backup instead of silently omitting them so the user\nnotices that the migration file would be incomplete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql9c2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeakQACIt2L6gSp/vKEJPdwxQ+vei\noL20WgLc7YjS7siz4GrBdU+pVeua1kovktLFB7npVNChXaHEhXZT9oyEGD24PvUv\nFVZwDMPSWXDN/MVan02Y2CcDRggCyAd29mbYLF41F1ZvWe4cZqaL3frwI0BAW1SA\nYg6UUYoM6gzfTQf/YBgP0Pw2Hyje5Or4t/AuNkcqWNklJPx2NHnNd0+cA7S18tSY\nsoKeKTWl5BupU2HZ4bz4+f0iOmQNoBvsV1NFrS61vz+W9ELZoD9hnTCtdbB16QLb\noQEErjP3/XImlf37TFDB2CWwf3K0hQfKhuYbqkYAkxHejf+tpknJCd67/cPFV8Ca\npH3rowqV0z6DE5F5lVTUozsQKf9dk/DYaH3NOdzTl36wlqJsiQaO8vuPYY1fj63n\nBVrY4PoEYHWTcxKZoLvtXmSwPK5fuQJHqWHYdHsqkqWE9qhgV55H2ShVtNMj4al3\n7RFdO8irwqLM8CkEPMwc7LASsddKhTxzH/mATg2n/B3qhTsTwU9/XreAIGghlzpP\nUcEm3tn4wG9Z/W9Y8x5HpE8kklqMyxW0dkl5aDLKIxy1AUeJ1/zFFisC1SJ0MYlr\nb+WpSGd6zCFmv38YI7zwBvYua6ADE0KCbir0X4JGf67mlcJkIX6/lkMoOquWAxNh\nrXVk45sSBzIRSc4qQYM5\n=n0UM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T07:58:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/5c32e566cbf7a0228e348700f658b7dac537d28f","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDVjMzJlNTY2Y2JmN2EwMjI4ZTM0ODcwMGY2NThiN2RhYzUzN2QyOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab","sha":"06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab"}],"sha":"5c32e566cbf7a0228e348700f658b7dac537d28f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/5c32e566cbf7a0228e348700f658b7dac537d28f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104281681?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tyagiquamar","id":104281681,"login":"Tyagiquamar","node_id":"U_kgDOBjc2UQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyagiquamar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:56:24Z","email":"104281681+Tyagiquamar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Mohd Quamar Tyagi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:56:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ldk): stop panicking on event-subscription close during shutdown (#2572)\n\n* fix(ldk): stop panicking on event-subscription close during shutdown\n\nSendPaymentSync, SendKeysend, and OpenChannel receive from the LDK event\nsubscription channel without checking the ok flag. When the node shuts down\nthe broadcaster closes the channel, the receive yields a nil *ldk_node.Event,\nand the type assertion/dereference on it panics. Check the ok flag and honor\nls.ctx in the previously-blocking OpenChannel wait so shutdown returns a\nclean error instead.\n\nAdds TestLDKEventBroadcaster_SubscriptionClosedOnShutdown and\nTestLDKEventBroadcaster_ContextCancelledWhileAwaiting.\n\n* fix(ldk): honor caller context in OpenChannel and PayOfferSync wait loops\n\nBoth functions accept a caller ctx but only selected on ls.ctx (service\nshutdown), so a caller cancellation stayed blocked until an event or\nshutdown. Add a ctx.Done() branch ahead of the service-shutdown branch.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit review on #2572.\n\n* fix(ldk): revert PayOfferSync changes, handled in a separate PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Roland Bewick <roland.bewick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf6aa1319c0299b32253084689e4133650053203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/bf6aa1319c0299b32253084689e4133650053203"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/06b8fd9ebd2e9a84b1648e9f55cf5914e09ba5ab","verification":{"payload":"tree bf6aa1319c0299b32253084689e4133650053203\nparent 11b233a0f72dc7c33516af6cb9b40b95dfc3d36e\nauthor Mohd Quamar Tyagi <104281681+Tyagiquamar@users.noreply.github.com> 1788328584 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788328584 +0700\n\nfix(ldk): stop panicking on event-subscription close during shutdown (#2572)\n\n* fix(ldk): stop panicking on event-subscription close during shutdown\n\nSendPaymentSync, SendKeysend, and OpenChannel receive from the LDK event\nsubscription channel without checking the ok flag. When the node shuts down\nthe broadcaster closes the channel, the receive yields a nil *ldk_node.Event,\nand the type assertion/dereference on it panics. Check the ok flag and honor\nls.ctx in the previously-blocking OpenChannel wait so shutdown returns a\nclean error instead.\n\nAdds TestLDKEventBroadcaster_SubscriptionClosedOnShutdown and\nTestLDKEventBroadcaster_ContextCancelledWhileAwaiting.\n\n* fix(ldk): honor caller context in OpenChannel and PayOfferSync wait loops\n\nBoth functions accept a caller ctx but only selected on ls.ctx (service\nshutdown), so a caller cancellation stayed blocked until an event or\nshutdown. Add a ctx.Done() branch ahead of the service-shutdown branch.\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit review on #2572.\n\n* fix(ldk): revert PayOfferSync changes, handled in a separate PR\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Roland Bewick <roland.bewick@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql7qICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhf0QACZuNVcOmMnmiUhQL2dGKh+9\nGgxbcIgqkr06eh5xJZlUAnutzVUwLi0xjs3fWg8lq6yHKj5n5290z9MWcQcPvpQt\nUMe5B+6O24Ny88Mu1cwqaUO1mbNWDXEbdq8UIVuft/zgNFHhUavO02kp9scbkCGO\nJ8wKtWJrvuKLFXPphLRDhacrAuaS3J6F97XQ+koz/BahihM6vG8WyRtYccfMCHry\nGADZrfkUcoczQ5eeK4h