by/hub/commit/edd283cdb2c38724657d196cc1ed7fb417bb60ed","sha":"edd283cdb2c38724657d196cc1ed7fb417bb60ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/edd283cdb2c38724657d196cc1ed7fb417bb60ed"}],"sha":"d2cebc5c6f8ed6df29c2afc2b61383ffad66f79e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/d2cebc5c6f8ed6df29c2afc2b61383ffad66f79e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/edd283cdb2c38724657d196cc1ed7fb417bb60ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T15:14:49Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T15:14:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: update encryption scheme for node migration files (#2539)\n\n* fix: update encryption scheme for node migration files\n\nMigration files are now encrypted with AES-CTR using a key derived via\nArgon2 with a 32-byte salt, the same derivation used for encrypted\nconfiguration values. Files created by earlier versions can still be\nrestored: the restore path detects the scheme by trial-decrypting the\narchive header and checking for the ZIP file signature, which also\nrejects an incorrect unlock password up front instead of extracting\ngarbage.\n\nThe migration screen now also tells users to never share their\nmigration file with anyone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: reword migration file warning\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: read full migration file header before detecting cipher scheme\n\nio.ReadAtLeast can return once the smallest scheme''s header is read,\nwhich truncates the larger current-scheme header when the reader\ndelivers short reads (e.g. a network request body). Read the full\nheader and only tolerate a short read that still covers the smallest\nscheme.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: extract migration files to a staging directory during restore\n\nIf extraction failed partway through, the partially populated restore\ndirectory was left in the working directory, and the next startup would\napply the incomplete restore. Extract to a staging directory and only\nmove it into place after every entry has been extracted successfully.\nAlso reject archives that contain no files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: assert traversal-specific error in restore backup test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe7f389cb1b89bd12beb2da9e9aa2a587473d9f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/fe7f389cb1b89bd12beb2da9e9aa2a587473d9f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/edd283cdb2c38724657d196cc1ed7fb417bb60ed","verification":{"payload":"tree fe7f389cb1b89bd12beb2da9e9aa2a587473d9f2\nparent 1c7abc62e91d75e021ad69b2128e46a1c33ac953\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786547689 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786547689 +0700\n\nfix: update encryption scheme for node migration files (#2539)\n\n* fix: update encryption scheme for node migration files\n\nMigration files are now encrypted with AES-CTR using a key derived via\nArgon2 with a 32-byte salt, the same derivation used for encrypted\nconfiguration values. Files created by earlier versions can still be\nrestored: the restore path detects the scheme by trial-decrypting the\narchive header and checking for the ZIP file signature, which also\nrejects an incorrect unlock password up front instead of extracting\ngarbage.\n\nThe migration screen now also tells users to never share their\nmigration file with anyone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: reword migration file warning\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: read full migration file header before detecting cipher scheme\n\nio.ReadAtLeast can return once the smallest scheme''s header is read,\nwhich truncates the larger current-scheme header when the reader\ndelivers short reads (e.g. a network request body). Read the full\nheader and only tolerate a short read that still covers the smallest\nscheme.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: extract migration files to a staging directory during restore\n\nIf extraction failed partway through, the partially populated restore\ndirectory was left in the working directory, and the next startup would\napply the incomplete restore. Extract to a staging directory and only\nmove it into place after every entry has been extracted successfully.\nAlso reject archives that contain no files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: assert traversal-specific error in restore backup test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfI3pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaYQQ