Q6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/3b3c37dd0ce87184b2f67b90864cf9288f8727b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:48:06Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T07:48:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remove legacy acceptance of empty unlock password check (#2534)\n\n* fix: remove legacy acceptance of empty unlock password check\n\nCheckUnlockPassword previously treated a missing or empty\nUnlockPasswordCheck value as a match — a legacy compatibility path from\nbefore the canary was always written. It now requires the stored value\nto be present and to equal the expected string.\n\nStartApp checks for the canary up front and, if it is missing, stops\nwith a message asking the user to restore from a backup rather than\ncontinuing. A new IsUnlockPasswordCheckSet helper reports whether the\nvalue is present.\n\nkeys.Init now returns the error from reading NostrSecretKey instead of\nignoring it, so a read failure aborts instead of generating and saving a\nnew key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add operation context to unlock password check errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"271417bdc7e91bde65c599310536b82aa94cddd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/271417bdc7e91bde65c599310536b82aa94cddd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/3b3c37dd0ce87184b2f67b90864cf9288f8727b1","verification":{"payload":"tree 271417bdc7e91bde65c599310536b82aa94cddd0\nparent 979644cf688282ee3c4014554be7215fb9e8f151\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786520886 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786520886 +0700\n\nfix: remove legacy acceptance of empty unlock password check (#2534)\n\n* fix: remove legacy acceptance of empty unlock password check\n\nCheckUnlockPassword previously treated a missing or empty\nUnlockPasswordCheck value as a match — a legacy compatibility path from\nbefore the canary was always written. It now requires the stored value\nto be present and to equal the expected string.\n\nStartApp checks for the canary up front and, if it is missing, stops\nwith a message asking the user to restore from a backup rather than\ncontinuing. A new IsUnlockPasswordCheckSet helper reports whether the\nvalue is present.\n\nkeys.Init now returns the error from reading NostrSecretKey instead of\nignoring it, so a read failure aborts instead of generating and saving a\nnew key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: add operation context to unlock password check errors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfCU2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoq4QAK9uemJo290uV/FFqB26NYLE\nwMhcNLZndJ24Z/3tmKdedCyuwQBego9hQ3NoQx9BsO1lkbBpRIGyCQp2YoQ6Q2f3\n+0l6KN2jevQ356Yvz7AZX5f4QmfEvxgf1K0QJtnSa6hAmRbnRfqk9KS2NzdAjN8l\n5YgFR83v401msWeXPEs/E3ElBLMIYj093RafcQqrLAtmW5i97r+U26dTIykNCoQx\nyvINj4EQS8zyznAHKEpnL+MhMFSxzZn7z4tc+/qv4n5fmvsd5lWCTH8eaD28sboG\nP6HLrEnD61J9CPF1fXG46HebsjJINYqUSOKNDVlUyffxKr9YvBEvJGvQls3LZTjz\nOEQug4QaUfT4OrzdB38Tf2/AxFq+2NLgwiUsLjbiMdfYNzyvh5GwNsThq+MH7t2D\nzwb7hRSAAlS8EyMkSTuJYurPBIsSTc8VCNuUhoW3IM6Bo6Nzhxik3ntWOojFzGND\nrFS3d7mc3