76513ce91a869ddd0a98dab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/4bcc1d108e52106a76513ce91a869ddd0a98dab8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/4402d2fff88b86c9e4136f616260ebb83d304074","verification":{"payload":"tree 4bcc1d108e52106a76513ce91a869ddd0a98dab8\nparent 5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786438166 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786438166 +0700\n\nfix: remove request bodies from error logs (#2533)\n\nThe Wails request router included the full request body in its error\nlog entries, and the HTTP app creation handler logged the whole request\nstruct on failure. Log only the route, method and error instead,\nmatching the existing behavior of the /api/mnemonic handler, and log\nonly the route and method for requests in the desktop frontend.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeuIWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwkMQABVaH4uBFNq0DZmbMtykQubn\nWP+2Z2tH7omxGLxR/K4JraCK8Hykz2ugzEQ83L0zdMtLtLVoI7qh9pF9v+wA4J08\nnQBqS/2xWLL6Qb/LZrmjZqk3u4sKqnb8t8llOhFnJHXSJZhbqg5+qq5GsUyBKS5F\nSWvuubqpygwaNDLusydOL8glOoD8iD7+qJWRxwsK3QZJGZiSy9ZI+hDR8dzn8kv2\npCHxNU9Jd/vpynB8MjVn99tMyjx57jbbyf/N4RHB0TS0SiJ1nWoDx7Z/TW2UiPBa\nwHF2cKYNYWtAo0gIQDXqaHWg1g2TtEgVI4M2kBQt/G5hns3PvJzhRzvGHXEy1zQJ\ntcG9ist92V9EEzhM1bExjboOyPOAAbMfgvx62EO+/Exp8Z+LqMFHmM8il7jfwhbS\neOMxD+BKjRJ9tmAW9Fqnl3vBHVwb+5Q5knlcH4GcVUWH4uBel0j+JwdPszbkkIfq\nZkiKQo6hXeS7rl35TY0ZMy2Esb8HAAFXT2mz3o0aiVZikCMF4qFhtDuLNWRsT7ye\nFJm+H+Q+x9wUCF7y1KXUAziWf3GutL6AJ2V1o6fjrLhj6JHoWWgRDpr6bKCiFMU5\nY1G2j0ec0mNChqdc3MfYDAMtUWGM6Qv/mkm6yZ9GDs4E1EVbumHWjM8+rouwPZnq\ntW2MOlviladQQJIjFiWc\n=lpXE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T08:50:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/4402d2fff88b86c9e4136f616260ebb83d304074","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDQ0MDJkMmZmZjg4Yjg2YzllNDEzNmY2MTYyNjBlYmI4M2QzMDQwNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd","sha":"5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd"}],"sha":"4402d2fff88b86c9e4136f616260ebb83d304074","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/4402d2fff88b86c9e4136f616260ebb83d304074"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:05:56Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T08:05:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: validate LND and CLN credential files during setup (#2528)\n\nThe setup API accepts file paths for the LND certificate and macaroon\nand for the CLN lightning directory. Previously the raw file contents\nwere read and stored without any validation.\n\nValidate these inputs before persisting them:\n\n- LND cert: parse the PEM and store only the re-encoded certificate(s),\n  discarding any other PEM blocks (e.g. a bundled private key).\n- LND macaroon: unmarshal and store the re-marshalled macaroon.\n- CLN lightning directory: verify it contains the TLS credentials\n  (ca.pem, client.pem, client-key.pem) that CLN loads at connect time,\n  including the hold subdirectory when configured.\n\nOn failure, return a generic error to the client and log the detail\nserver-side. File paths remain supported for Umbrel-style installs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36c1c41a0179092949ecd083d35c56329075002b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/36c1c41a0179092949ecd083d35c56329075002b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/5f9a88843cc13eb401b3bc8c45156425b222e8bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 36c1c41a0179092949ecd083d35c56329075002b\nparent 3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786435556 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786435556 +0700\n\nfix: validate LND and CLN credential files during setup (#2528)\n\nThe setup API accepts file paths for the LND certificate and macaroon\nand for the CLN lightning directory. Previously the raw file contents\nwere read and stored without any validation.\n\nValidate these inputs before persisting them:\n\n- LND cert: parse the PEM and store only the re-encoded certificate(s),\n  discarding any other PEM blocks (e.g. a bundled private key).\n- LND macaroon: unmarshal and store the re-marshalled macaroon.\n- CLN lightning directory: verify it contains the TLS credentials\n  (ca.pem, client.pem, client-key.pem) that CLN loads at connect time,\n  including the hold subdirectory when configured.\n\nOn failure, return a generic error to the client and log the detail\nserver-side. File paths remain supported for Umbrel-style installs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqetfkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxYEQAD33F+JDeqjA/Ce0f1R+xmRK\nw69d3B99Ye+1t+PTzFNPGAL+Fyy0UnFxf5t54CsptEudjvYVYWqeftZf8Uam9eNY\n2ZZvfLqhqBYbGuLY1rHekaEiEihVqh825yK22MtD5txQd+RsnVCvGNUPln1cJSbE\nEb5NJaT4nN7OnV8zKMZYtyxkd+mBOdD/gks59txLN6uMuEXi3JfXXYZUgl7PJXUB\nHJDRD1zHt17mvLsOAoSYoQlyzu7BWFPTBnWPOSHdmXu4725gIQPUzWygDrVh48TV\n2og8IHf9l2t7GeD1hVTSiUSgP9Ce0B4lCttzpoRO+F+TpPzNysWPebzS3l0hqubT\n2/ekflcgnu10hjBlYpBCdjhqHTcojaYU8rgwJ6zbZz8GSHXUpo5Xc+XKxgqGU2wH\noDB9uQRboUcAgNqv6Ib6Gdl1BueJDa+ad8CkXb2BIljxl7YmkxbP1pyQkIDN/E9q\n6V8i0JA50m9MT+qcIA0ld4I2FClz2cGULpNMwxonpRJ3xvsD38xU53x37WPGyGy3\nj1CBCXyg5o2x9bBxIbJD8yroFeI8oU7csDTG4+8cMe0ceTaWbzyAwoB60IQNAn1I\n2800g2F9QWuhhyvIL5R7WpuggzYcjxCyGzbV3mhb/m/ZFpv1yB2ZIQSPCSLpl+Ay\nOkoyrqRRW3M33sDgX2q1\n=0I58\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T08:06:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/priva