"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T07:57:51Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T07:57:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: validate return_to redirect URLs (#2532)\n\nreturn_to query parameters are now parsed and only http and https URLs\nare used for redirects, both in the frontend and when the createApp API\nadds the connection parameters to the URL.\n\nThe production frontend build now also includes the same\nContent-Security-Policy meta tag that is served as a header in http\nmode, so the policy also applies where no HTTP headers are set, e.g. in\nthe desktop app.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"967fc0429a52618e5b35aa27a9f0f0aa57ecf5c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/967fc0429a52618e5b35aa27a9f0f0aa57ecf5c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875","verification":{"payload":"tree 967fc0429a52618e5b35aa27a9f0f0aa57ecf5c1\nparent 0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786435071 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786435071 +0700\n\nfix: validate return_to redirect URLs (#2532)\n\nreturn_to query parameters are now parsed and only http and https URLs\nare used for redirects, both in the frontend and when the createApp API\nadds the connection parameters to the URL.\n\nThe production frontend build now also includes the same\nContent-Security-Policy meta tag that is served as a header in http\nmode, so the policy also applies where no HTTP headers are set, e.g. in\nthe desktop app.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqetX/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+lsQAIm5ibtj1pRM7UcgzW6NipIj\nyneYPVpcwMWKCNZcK2TlaJH6BJ4OISJqpP58TWIlwp8iqmrQ9kVU/9vy7l66HIS4\nCyEpypbY9R9PPPmsSlDlTBG/CRfaVEGbNZierM048HD1tiiB6QXFVSBkiTVbOKn3\nsuVQpD1ajDWhYzuBwFYMMKXiIV9dqObmQmYboq6Txti9F9MLnrw/b11bDiLpa2a1\nT/beZbHpvxSHzH7fXUziPX93/7AxTn/iN+yTHivCNmBFDEbqA/FF37OT5rVJrS+E\nFL4d+evgVgfUTTn8KUjAO4HUrQDP+8EFJz/Jw7sM+ry/rFhTzWydhJWXgq+cCkSv\nEy8gxDjAy/ltX5sify2gTKUNys+LcxI4iAlbFI6rhPbDLYs1I0G4bPyzkEK4W5Rd\n1pvkHY4F0bCyWV0k7YtgUi0RU9sebH+4Plw8Co+DDh263saSmdQxKua/t7A6klXg\ntVcwMnxO6/i2tGxhq5ZkyjHjwuMBDSiGmzGNsMBJX5qMmOQu8pbuXOao3DYPBKLF\n0E618EyMxDT6cvnOO1aSBUK4llU1H1GkRfT1HSvsaMGf9WBMXq66dUoWIXJv2mL6\nBOBpbubACuwx7FqgP0CObVvyrhz7JkeeRfzRFuRuCuVGRW94OL561Uqdf/QkUTi1\nkEj09Aa1ThyD5tTewSHN\n=tm/H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T07:58:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDNkMjI5OTMzODk3YTEzYjU2ZjVkZGNmNjA3MzRkZmEzMDBmZTg4NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d","sha":"0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d"}],"sha":"3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/3d229933897a13b56f5ddcf60734dfa300fe8875"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T07:48:41Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T07:48:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make event assertions in tests wait for async event consumption (#2531)\n\nThe mock event consumer waited a fixed 10ms before returning consumed\nevents, which was not always enough on slow CI runners and caused flaky\nfailures (e.g. TestMarkSettled_App_BudgetWarning missing its\nnwc_budget_warning event). It also appended to the events slice from\nconcurrent goroutines without synchronization, a data race that could\ndrop events.\n\n- guard the consumed events slice with a mutex and return copies\n- add WaitForConsumedEvents which polls until the expected number of\n  events arrived (up to 5s) instead of relying on a fixed sleep\n- use it in tests that assert on consumed events; tests asserting that\n  no event was published keep the short grace period\n- normalize event order in the keysend self-payment test, matching the\n  existing approach in the self-payment test, since async publishing\n  does not guarantee ordering\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"202ae375fb3b1082a28ac0264abe7e84576de426","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/202ae375fb3b1082a28ac0264abe7e84576de426"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d","verification":{"payload":"tree 202ae375fb3b1082a28ac0264abe7e84576de426\nparent fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786434521 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786434521 +0700\n\nfix: make event assertions in tests wait for async event consumption (#2531)\n\nThe mock event consumer waited a fixed 10ms before returning consumed\nevents, which was not always enough on slow CI runners and caused flaky\nfailures (e.g. TestMarkSettled_App_BudgetWarning missing its\nnwc_budget_warning event). It also appended to the events slice from\nconcurrent goroutines without synchronization, a data race that could\ndrop events.\n\n- guard the consumed events slice with a mutex and return copies\n- add WaitForConsumedEvents which polls until the expected number of\n  events arrived (up to 5s) instead of relying on a fixed sleep\n- use it in tests that assert on consumed events; tests asserting that\n  no event was published keep the short grace period\n- normalize event order in the keysend self-payment test, matching the\n  existing approach in the self-payment test, since async publishing\n  does not guarantee ordering\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqetPZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUmkQAIQpr8/ZEDVbDPaYW1MOrDE9\nq13vVMIheLfv0P/OrnxPeg/Wvjw8apRERX8RKzdJfarGGBtIRy4Im3hNOe1eoh8K\n9+CLPhYiVFwcJL+LL2wYuVsMD8eNKTX81bLymRX6wN517k2CucKzbDm3GagB5Tfj\nOxzIKXN/xTDx3QqJh/JRGjC25uQQc8w7xQ6fJiq7+rG+WhiZjh9xovB24z10Kjer\n6D75aOEDiW9FRCt/apSbyish/PA/EX9lzGL7X0jtyu1+Ds8NEnXM7J1bAZTqGGT8\nXEpzqTDc/T4qz51j+YNnc0MUYhfXNK3y03xq+XQ8u1q2dJNIRKUtJuAf1107Qv3c\nOAQrFhKHX+EmoXV4nRKtKDfvfkesBbUcFJUr/N/wnTiBpSK+9Hl0eUA109LrMyH8\n3Hxig4vgc5bN45qxyXeKK9BcVnCA3u5q+4M2I1UHpT8eeXQ/gMjivQe2r9N/7Kpb\nZMrK9f4NYqFfhybZCjh0EhVG6JhQVf4bB3HRjqY4nISAkoP74ju88tXiroFJSEXG\n+VDfFIPAxJrM5jhIYvBtPyAEP2wmQb8d0p4l4XQE5EssJQi48N/i8sIahkV5KbS2\ngFpyozdpZnHjFa+B6TW69SXo1ohlATFqxAlHnqFsjYGwpNjMaMO79CcrxZHr2RnP\nUjJ174t10yLJ0hiMqO7C\n=/fwN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T07:49:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKDBiMGNiYmQ5ODViNzVhNTliMjgyNzg5YTcwNzdiODczOWFlNzcxNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c","sha":"fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c"}],"sha":"0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/0b0cbbd985b75a59b282789a7077b8739ae7716d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:42:45Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:42:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: prevent backup restore from writing outside the restore directory (#2529)\n\nArchive entry names come from the uploaded backup and were joined to the\nrestore directory without validation, so an entry name containing \"..\"\nsegments could resolve to a path outside it. Reject entries whose name is\nabsolute or escapes the restore directory, and confirm the cleaned\ndestination path stays within it before writing.\n\nAdd a test covering rejection of an entry that points outside the restore\ndirectory.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"08ce1220da83820cef1dc4aefe18325a0d4b367b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/08ce1220da83820cef1dc4aefe18325a0d4b367b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/fa5cc3511e5f0507d6de67644f4bbf28b002088c","verification":{"payload":"tree 08ce1220da83820cef1dc4aefe18325a0d4b367b\nparent 037765794d026623544c19dc38d34cf722564c40\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786380165 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786380165 +0700\n\nfix: prevent backup restore from writing outside the restore directory (#2529)\n\nArchive entry names come from the uploaded backup and were joined to the\nrestore directory without validation, so an entry name containing \"..\"\nsegments could resolve to a path outside it. Reject entries whose name is\nabsolute or escapes the restore directory, and confirm the cleaned\ndestination path stays within it before writing.\n\nAdd a test covering rejection of an entry that points outside the restore\ndirectory.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqef+FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXSIQAJaP0oh904xQE9fWpUqXVPRw\np/oa8Hgdvq8GWD3B0JS1eqr8SkG0TMOWNFA/kSCN1TIXATyMcuXIs/Vu0cc6vV2P\nolccHVgQOS3DqBP3H+eoKr3ECPYAPv2lBjd4wg5sai