/api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/ffee8cbcbeab3969654604a45076af8e094a523a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T07:20:41Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T07:20:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: enable migration from postgres to sqlite (#2524)\n\nAllows users running Alby Hub on postgres (e.g. Alby Cloud) to create a\nmigration file from Settings -> Migrate Alby Hub. The contents of the\npostgres database are copied into a temporary local sqlite database\nwhich is included in the migration file, so it can be imported into a\nfresh sqlite-based hub.\n\n- extract the db_migrate CLI copy logic into a shared db.MigrateDB\n- also copy the swaps and forwards tables (previously silently dropped)\n- only require VSS in the source when migrating to postgres\n- show a hint on the migrate page when running on postgres\n- show database storage type and VSS status on the about page\n- don''t log an error when removing non-existent db files before restore\n\nCloses #2500\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"478eabe67732cb32ccdf7e480a6c3e2ec4d1dc9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/478eabe67732cb32ccdf7e480a6c3e2ec4d1dc9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/ffee8cbcbeab3969654604a45076af8e094a523a","verification":{"payload":"tree 478eabe67732cb32ccdf7e480a6c3e2ec4d1dc9b\nparent 6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786346441 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786346441 +0700\n\nfeat: enable migration from postgres to sqlite (#2524)\n\nAllows users running Alby Hub on postgres (e.g. Alby Cloud) to create a\nmigration file from Settings -> Migrate Alby Hub. The contents of the\npostgres database are copied into a temporary local sqlite database\nwhich is included in the migration file, so it can be imported into a\nfresh sqlite-based hub.\n\n- extract the db_migrate CLI copy logic into a shared db.MigrateDB\n- also copy the swaps and forwards tables (previously silently dropped)\n- only require VSS in the source when migrating to postgres\n- show a hint on the migrate page when running on postgres\n- show database storage type and VSS status on the about page\n- don''t log an error when removing non-existent db files before restore\n\nCloses #2500\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeXvJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArFUQAJqRmoxWv5huPYjbfN8Zz08/\ncfmU5mij27K7l3EIrnNqBOMVlSO47IMLK2rnwFzaJ3vhx7mJDB+OgZgmT+7fRn+s\nFaFAZ2wAcWTfc6GgZOKTMfhiYeKRUXj9RufVnBf+/kpQDg+bw7n/oy0i73OyhwCP\nxMp+zRUwMg/Ar12rzNpwEI2vgPSNl/yMdzZU4Pd2mSFpbyMK2U0yHJDvRTXjKVpM\nNQXUxwJ0lpx9OzsGZey8KjXkAHsAds20M+4lq1mIHN2Bjich8cCGL/Hc33MpriEm\ntw1XMkRLU5ALX4x49/dignGuml4STnR0HpMLjyQDHTVtMmC174ZOF0JFXdo8U4St\nMEnMTc6mC+31MraFTGUF8PRzFFG/pA4TvPtCfJWbaTgmPA5l7QxJfEJoqE9ZTGrw\nYcHoH1K7eCIUtNI6JfUfWLRrPsQ55zfjzKYdK+usrPl/duL6ZSFiEzCntxQQr2yD\nhWLQLMygimE1+vJ7lKnOVgAJEh2FlyWANidpzZmbhdEEsxwKZTgp5beglHWx56Ql\n8tnkwIxGDEWRQ3yaK2yHznxh8FngC9V0wirxRhfInJ+lCCQDZA4wIaAOpmWs4mGN\nP4dGouCJgQIfPH6Y5Lz5WMXxMaikrEjQZWs77J14G7uGn9FQxTFrYs1hDFuayNB/\nbZqYo5LwuJ01rwg1OqLr\n=bM5K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T07:20:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/ffee8cbcbeab3969654604a45076af8e094a523a","node_id":"C_kwDOMSPVeNoAKGZmZWU4Y2JjYmVhYjM5Njk2NTQ2MDRhNDUwNzZhZjhlMDk0YTUyM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/getAlby/hub/commit/6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af","sha":"6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af"}],"sha":"ffee8cbcbeab3969654604a45076af8e094a523a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/ffee8cbcbeab3969654604a45076af8e094a523a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33993199?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rolznz","id":33993199,"login":"rolznz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTkzMTk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rolznz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/commits/6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T09:39:02Z","email":"33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Roland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T09:39:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: bark onboarding, migration messaging and receive settlement for bark 0.6.0 (#2523)\n\n* fix: update bark onboarding and backup messaging for seed-based recovery\n\nSince bark 0.6.0, offchain funds are recoverable from the mnemonic\nalone via the seed-derived recovery mailbox. Remove the outdated\nwarnings that the recovery phrase is not sufficient, show the standard\nrecovery guidance for bark during onboarding, and expose the\nseed-recovery scan result as a ''recoveryreport'' custom node command so\nusers migrating to a new device can verify their funds were restored.\n\nCloses #2512\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: settle bark lightning receives in the new delivering state\n\nbark 0.6.0 added a ''delivering'' receive state between preimage reveal\nand settlement. The receive claim handler only treated\n''preimage-revealed'' and ''settled'' as paid, so claimed receives were\npublished without a preimage and the transactions service rejected the\nsettlement (''no preimage in payment''), leaving paid invoices pending\nforever.\n\nRecognize all states at or past preimage reveal via a receiveIsPaid\nhelper (a positive allowlist, so an unknown future state degrades to\npending rather than falsely settled), only mark the transaction settled\nwhen the preimage is present, and prefer bark''s own settled_at\ntimestamp when available.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: replace import channels checkbox with LDK-specific warning\n\nThe ''I don''t have another Alby Hub to migrate or open channels''\ncheckbox on the import recovery phrase screen only applied to LDK but\nwas required for every backend, and its claim that channel funds are\nalways lost is wrong when dynamic channel backups (VSS) are enabled.\n\nRemove the checkbox and the channels bullet from the import screen and\nshow the caveat on the Security & Recovery page instead, only when a\nmnemonic was imported and the LDK backend was chosen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d797c991f4c1100f2d6bb9a0befe55cbc7149c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/trees/d797c991f4c1100f2d6bb9a0befe55cbc7149c07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/getAlby/hub/git/commits/6d0cb6fd2c0088463f64e75f7309a8859c9ed9af","verification":{"payload":"tree d797c991f4c1100f2d6bb9a0befe55cbc7149c07\nparent d198b19bef49851e6a04ecc609be89dfdc893464\nauthor Roland <33993199+rolznz@users.noreply.github.com> 1786181942 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786181942 +0700\n\nfix: bark onboarding, migration messaging and receive settlement for bark 0.6.0 (#2523)\n\n* fix: update bark onboarding and backup messaging for seed-based recovery\n\nSince bark 0.6.0, offchain funds are recoverable from the mnemonic\nalone via the seed-derived recovery mailbox. Remove the outdated\nwarnings that the recovery phrase is not sufficient, show the standard\nrecovery guidance for bark during onboarding, and expose the\nseed-recovery scan result as a ''recoveryreport'' custom node command so\nusers migrating to a new device can verify their funds were restored.\n\nCloses #2512\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: settle bark lightning receives in the new delivering state\n\nbark 0.6.0 added a ''delivering'' receive state between preimage reveal\nand settlement. The receive claim handler only treated\n''preimage-revealed'' and ''settled'' as paid, so claimed receives were\npublished without a preimage and the transactions service rejected the\nsettlement (''no preimage in payment''), leaving paid invoices pending\nforever.\n\nRecognize all states at or past preimage reveal via a receiveIsPaid\nhelper (a positive allowlist, so an unknown future state degrades to\npending rather than falsely settled), only mark the transaction settled\nwhen the preimage is present, and prefer bark''s own settled_at\ntimestamp when available.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: replace import channels checkbox with LDK-specific warning\n\nThe ''I don''t have another Alby Hub to migrate or open channels''\ncheckbox on the import recovery phrase screen only applied to LDK but\nwas required for every backend, and its claim that channel funds are\nalways lost is wrong when dynamic channel backups (VSS) are enabled.\n\nRemove the checkbox and the channels bullet from the import screen and\nshow the caveat on the Security & Recovery page instead, only when a\nmnemonic was imported and the LDK backend was chosen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdvk2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg6QQABLNBOiGpmkbt3bsBA7ByP1E\n8GTIAthGAAJbun2exMFVIt/kMsRC4hl5/PE6R8Fqs8+aQncAbbsdcZZ5T49L/sIn\nJ+Y1epuhaoM4hR+FwTm2oT1CXOuwYTurK9OviOsjM5WJTC9eNm6xiZWWryfCgNRH\nZa7KYyM3B+qB5Ez2LwBvQv7KJiEY6mPQcEkcGq6jkiLKSk+z5IsJJwjEGVd9iLjN\nozEJycapub7kFq0ihr6GYzPchWAn/wZHEfdjn3cdX2+Ft0